\par }\pard\plain \s444\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12861300 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf9\insrsid11612319 King Par\'e9k\'f1it inquired from \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9:}{
\fs28\insrsid11612319  O great sage, why did King Priyavrata, who was a great, self-realized devotee of the Lord, remain in household life, which is the root cause of the bondage of karma [fruitive activities] and which defeats the mission of human life?

\par }\pard\plain \s439\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10829270 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In the Fourth Canto, \'c7r\'e9la \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 explains that N\'e4
rada Muni perfectly instructed King Priyavrata about the mission of human life. The mission of human life is to realize one's self and then gradually to go back home, back to Godhead. Since N\'e4rada Muni instructed the King fully on this sub
ject, why did he again enter household life, which is the main cause of material bondage? Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1
it was greatly astonished that King Priyavrata remained in household life, especially since he was not only a self-realized soul but also a first-class
 devotee of the Lord. A devotee actually has no attraction for household life, but surprisingly, King Priyavrata enjoyed household life very much. One may argue, "Why is it wrong to enjoy household life?" The reply is that in household life one becomes bo
u
nd by the results of fruitive activities. The essence of household life is sense enjoyment, and as long as one engrosses his mind in working hard for sense enjoyment, one becomes bound by the reactions of fruitive activities. This ignorance of self-realiz
ation is the greatest defeat in human life. The human form of life is especially meant for getting out of the bondage of fruitive activities, but as long as one is forgetful of his life's mission and acts like an ordinary animal\emdash 
eating, sleeping, mating and defending\emdash he must continue his conditioned life of material existence. Such a life is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 svar\'fcpa-vism\'e5ti,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 forgetfulness of one's real constitutional position. Therefore in Vedic civilization one is trained in the very beginning of life as a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahmac\'e4r\'e9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  A }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahmac\'e4r\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  must execute austerities and refrain from sex indulgence. Therefore if one is completely trained in the principles of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahmacarya,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  he generally does not enter household life. He is then called a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nai\'f1\'f6hika-brahmac\'e4r\'e9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  which indicates total celibacy. King Par\'e9k\'f1
it was thus astonished that the great King Priyavrata, although trained in the principles of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nai\'f1\'f6hika-brahmacarya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  entered household life.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 The words }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bh\'e4gavata \'e4tm\'e4r\'e4ma\'f9
}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are very significant in this verse. If one is self-satisfied as is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bh\'e4gavata \'e4tm\'e4r\'e4ma\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 There are different types of satisfaction. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Karm\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are satisfied in their fruitive activities, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 are satisfied to merge into the effulgence of Brahman, and devotees are satisfied to engage in the Lord's service. The Lord is self-satisfied because He is fully opulent, and one who is satisfied by serving Him is called }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bh\'e4gavata \'e4tm\'e4r\'e4ma\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Manu\'f1y\'e4\'eb\'e4\'e0 sahasre\'f1u:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 out of many thousands of persons, one may endeavor for liberation, and of man
y thousands of persons attempting to become liberated, one may achieve liberation from the anxieties of material existence and become self-satisfied. Even that satisfaction, however, is not the ultimate satisfaction. The }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karm\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  have desires, as do the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yog\'e9s,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  but devotees have no desires. Satisfaction in the service of the Lord is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ak\'e4ma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  freedom from desire, and this is the ultimate satisfaction. Therefore Mah
\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it inquired, "How could one who was fully satisfied on the highest platform be satisfied with family life?"
\par The word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 par\'e4bhava\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  in this verse is also significant. When one is satisfied in family life, he is doomed because he must already have forgotten his relationship with the Lord. Prahl
\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja describes how the activities of family life implicate one more and more. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c4tma-p\'e4ta\'e0 g\'e5ham andha-k\'fcpam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 household life is like a dark well. If one falls into this well, his spiritual death is assured. How Priyavrata Mah\'e4r\'e4ja remained a liberated }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 paramaha\'e0sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  even within family
 life is described in the next verse.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.1.2
