\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 paramaha\'e0sa}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash liberated persons; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 dayita}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash pleasing; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 kath\'e4m}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash glorification; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 ki\'efcit}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash sometimes; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 antar\'e4ya}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by impediments; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 vihat\'e4m}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash checked; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 sv\'e4m}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash own; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 \'e7iva-tam\'e4m}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash most exalted; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 padav\'e9m}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash position; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 na}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash do not; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 pr\'e4ye\'eba}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash almost always; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 hinvanti}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash give up.
\par }\pard\plain \s405\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3017748 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid2301602\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid2301602 
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf9\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said:}{
\fs28\insrsid11612319  What you have said is correct. The glories of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is praised in eloquent, transcendental verses by such exalted personalities as Brahm\'e4
, are very pleasing to great devotees and liberated persons. One who is attached to the nectarean honey of the Lord's lotus feet, and whose mind is 
always absorbed in His glories, may sometimes be checked by some impediment, but he still never gives up the exalted position he has acquired.
\par }\pard\plain \s439\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10829270 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 accepted both of the King's propositions
\emdash that a person who is advanced in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness cannot embrace materialistic life again and that one who has embraced materialistic life cannot take up K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness at any stage of his existence. Although accepting both these statements, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 qualified them by saying that a 
person who has once absorbed his mind in the glories of the Supreme Personality of Godhead may sometimes be influenced by impediments, but he still does not give up his exalted devotional position.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 According to \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura, there ar
e two kinds of impediments to devotional service. The first is an offense at the lotus feet of a Vai\'f1\'ebava. This is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vai\'f1\'ebava-apar\'e4dha.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu warned His devotees not to commit }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vai\'f1\'ebava-apar\'e4dha,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  which He described as the mad elephant
 offense. When a mad elephant enters a beautiful garden, it destroys everything, leaving a barren field. Similarly, the power of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vai\'f1\'ebava-apar\'e4dha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 is so great that even an advanced devotee becomes almost devoid of his spiritual assets if he commits it. Since K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness is eternal, it cannot be destroyed altogether, but advancement may be checked for the time being. Thus }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vai\'f1\'ebava-apar\'e4dha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is one kind of impediment to devotional service. Sometimes, however, the Supreme Personality of Godhead or His d
evotee desires to impede one's devotional service. For example, Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu and Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a were formerly Jaya and Vijaya, the gatekeepers in Vaiku\'eb\'f6
ha, but by the desire of the Lord, they became His enemies for three lives. Thus the desire of the Lord is another kind of impediment. But in both cases, the pure devotee, once advanced in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, cannot be lost. Following the orders of his superiors (Sv\'e4yambhuva and Lord Brahm\'e4), Priyavrata accepted family life, but this did not mean he lost his position in devotional service. K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness is perfect and eternal, and therefore it cannot be lost under any circumstances. Because the material world is full of obstructions to advancement in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, there may appear to be many impediments, yet K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, declares in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 9.31}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 kaunteya pratij\'e4n\'e9
hi na me bhakta\'f9 pra\'eba\'e7yati:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  once one has taken shelter at the lotus feet of the Lord, he cannot be lost.
\par In this verse, the word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7ivatam\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is very significant. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7ivatam\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 means "the most auspicious." The devotional path is so auspicious that a devotee cannot be lost under any circumstances. This is described in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 by the Lord Himself. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10490238 P}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e4rtha naiveha n\'e4mutra vin\'e4\'e7as tasya vidyate:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  
"My dear Arjuna, for a devotee there is no question of being lost, either in this life or in the next." }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (Bg. 6.40)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  In }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}
{\cf1\insrsid11612319 6.43}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ) the Lord clearly explains how this is so.
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 tatra ta\'e0 buddhi-sa\'e0yoga\'e0\line labhate paurva-dehikam\line 
yatate ca tato bh\'fcya\'f9\line sa\'e0siddhau kuru-nandana
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
By the order of the Lord, a perfect devotee sometimes comes to this material world like an ordinary human being. Because of his previous practice, such a perfect devotee naturally becomes attached to devotional service, apparently witho
ut cause. Despite all kinds of impediments due to surrounding circumstances, he automatically perseveres in devotional service and gradually advances until he once again becomes perfect. Bilvama\'ecgala \'d6h\'e4
kura had been an advanced devotee in his previous lif
e, but in his next life he became greatly fallen and was attached to a prostitute. Suddenly, however, his entire behavior was changed by the words of the very prostitute who had so much attracted him, and he became a great devotee. In the lives of exalted
 devotees, there are many such instances, proving that once one has taken to the shelter of the lotus feet of the Lord, he cannot be lost (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 kaunteya pratij\'e4n\'e9hi na me bhakta\'f9 pra\'eba\'e7yati}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 The fact is, however, that one becomes a devotee when he is completely
 freed from all reactions to sinful life. As K\'e5\'f1\'eba states in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 7.28}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ):
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 ye\'f1\'e4\'e0 tv anta-gata\'e0 p\'e4pa\'e0\line jan\'e4n\'e4\'e0 pu\'ebya-karma
\'eb\'e4m\line te dvanda-moha-nirmukt\'e4\line bhajante m\'e4\'e0 d\'e5\'f2ha-vrat\'e4\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "Persons who have acted piously in previous lives and in this life, whose 
sinful actions are completely eradicated and who are freed from the duality of illusion, engage themselves in My service with determination." On the other hand, as Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja said:
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 matir na k\'e5\'f1\'ebe parata\'f9 }{\insrsid11370492 svato v\'e4\line 
mitho 'bhipadyeta g\'e5ha}{\insrsid11612319 vrat\'e4n\'e4m
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 A person who is too attached to materialistic family life\emdash 
home, family, wife, children and so on\emdash cannot develop K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
