not to be rejected for any reason; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 tat-adhikara\'ebe}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash in occupying that post; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 \'e4tmana\'f9}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash of himself; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 anyasm\'e4t}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by other engagements; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 asata\'f9}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash material; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 api}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash certainly; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 par\'e4bhavam}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash deterioration; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 anv\'e9k\'f1am\'e4\'eba\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash foreseeing.
\par }\pard\plain \s405\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3017748 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid2301602\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid2301602 
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf9\insrsid11612319 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued:}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 
 My dear King, Prince Priyavrata was a great devotee because he sought the lotus feet of N\'e4rada, his spiritual master, and thus achieved the highest perfection in transcendental knowledge. With advanced knowledge, he always engaged in 
discussing spiritual subjects and did not divert his attention to anything else. The Prince's father then asked him to take charge of ruling the world. He tried to convince Priyavrata that this was his duty as indicated in the revealed scriptures. Prince 
P
riyavrata, however, was continuously practicing bhakti-yoga by constantly remembering the Supreme Personality of Godhead, thus engaging all his senses in the service of the Lord. Therefore, although the order of his father could not be rejected, the Princ
e did not welcome it. Thus he very conscientiously raised the question of whether he might be diverted from devotional service by accepting the responsibility of ruling over the world.
\par }\pard\plain \s439\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10829270 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9la Narottama d\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura has sung, }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ch\'e4\'f2iy\'e4 vai\'f1\'ebava-sev\'e4 nist\'e4ra p\'e4yeche keb\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "Without serving the lotus feet of a pure Vai\'f1\'eb
ava or spiritual master, no one has ever attained perfect liberation from material bondage." }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid3111552 P}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 rince Priyavrata regularly served the lotus feet of N\'e4rada, and thus the Prince perfectly unders
tood transcendental subjects in truth (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sa-tattva\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). The word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sa-tattva\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 means that Priyavrata knew all the facts about the spirit soul, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and the relationship between the spirit soul and the Supreme Personality of Godhead,
 and he also knew all about this material world and the relationship of the spirit soul and the Supreme Lord within the material world. Thus the Prince decided to engage himself only in rendering service to the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 When Priyavrata's father, Sv\'e4yambhuva M
anu, requested him to accept the responsibility of ruling over the world, he did not welcome the suggestion. This is the symptom of a great, liberated devotee. Even though engaged in worldly affairs, he does not take pleasure in them, but remains always a
b
sorbed in the Lord's service. While thus serving the Lord, he deals externally with worldly affairs without being affected. For example, although he has no attraction for his children, he cares for them and educates them to become devotees. Similarly, he 
speaks to his wife with affectionate words, but he is not attached to her. By rendering devotional service, a devotee acquires all the good qualities of the Supreme Lord. Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a had sixteen thousand wives, all of them very beautiful, and although He dea
lt with each of them as a beloved husband, He was not attracted or attached to any of them. In the same way, although a devotee may enter family life and act very affectionately toward his wife and children, he is never attached to these activities.

\par This verse states that by serving the lotus}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid3111552  feet of his spiritual master, P}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 rince Priyavrata very soon attained the perfectional stage of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness. This is the only way to advance in spiritual life. As stated in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas:
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 yasya deve par\'e4 bhaktir\line yath\'e4 deve tath\'e4 gurau\line tasyaite kathit
\'e4 hy arth\'e4\'f9\line prak\'e4\'e7ante mah\'e4tmana\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"If one has unflinching faith in the Supreme Lord and the spiritual master, the essence of all Vedic knowledge is revealed to him. (}{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7vet\'e4\'e7vatara Upani\'f1ad}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 6.23) A devotee always thinks of the Lord continuously. While chanting the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mantra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the words K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a and Hare immediately remind him of all the Lord's activities. Since his entire life is engaged in the service of the Lord, a devotee cannot forget the Lord at any time. Just as an o
rdinary man always engages his mind in material activities, a devotee always engages his mind in spiritual activities. This is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahma-satra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 or meditating upon the Supreme Lord always. Prince Priyavrata was perfectly initiated into this practice by \'c7r\'e9 N\'e4rada.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.1.7
