\emdash thus; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 ha}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash indeed; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 bhagav\'e4n}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash the most powerful; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 \'e4di-deva\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash the first demigod; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 etasya}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash of this universe; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 gu\'eba-visargasya}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash the creation of the three modes of material nature; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 parib\'e5\'e0ha\'eba}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash the welfare; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 anudhy\'e4na}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash always thinking of; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 vyavasita}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash known; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 sakala}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash whole; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 jagat}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash of the universe; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 abhipr\'e4ya\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by whom the ultimate purpose; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 \'e4tma}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash the Supreme Self; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 yoni\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash whose source of birth; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 akhila}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash all; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 nigama}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by the }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 Vedas;}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977  }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 nija-ga\'eba}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by personal associates; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 parive\'f1\'f6ita\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash being surrounded; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 sva-bhavan\'e4t}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash 
from his own abode; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 avatat\'e4ra}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash descended.
\par }\pard\plain \s405\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3017748 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid2301602\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid2301602 
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf9\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued:}{
\fs28\insrsid11612319  The first created being and most powerful demigod in this universe is Lord Brahm\'e4
, who is always responsible for developing universal affairs. Born directly from the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he dedicates his activities to the welfare of the entire universe, for he knows the purpose of the universal creation. This sup
remely powerful Lord Brahm\'e4, accompanied by his associates and the personified Vedas, left his own abode in the highest planetary system and descended to the place of Prince Priyavrata's meditation.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, the Supreme Self (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e4tm
\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), is the source of everything, as explained in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 janm\'e4dy asya yata\'f9.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Because Brahm\'e4 was born directly from Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, he is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e4tma-yoni.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is also called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhagav\'e4n,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  although generally }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhagav\'e4n}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  refers to the Supreme Personality of Godhead (Vi\'f1\'ebu or Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba). Sometimes great personalities\emdash 
such as demigods like Lord Brahm\'e4, N\'e4rada or Lord \'c7iva\emdash are also addressed as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhagav\'e4n}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  because they carry out the purpose of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Lord Brahm
\'e4 is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhagav\'e4n}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  because he is the sec
ondary creator of this universe. He is always thinking of how to improve the situation of the conditioned souls who have come to the material world to enjoy material activities. For this reason, he disseminates the Vedic knowledge throughout the universe 
for everyone's guidance.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedic knowledge is divided into two parts: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
prav\'e5tti-m\'e4rga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 niv\'e5tti-m\'e4rga.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Niv\'e5tti-m\'e4rga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 is the path of negating sense enjoyment, and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 prav\'e5tti-m\'e4rga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is the path by which the living entities are given a chance to enjoy and at the s
ame time are directed in such a way that they can go back home, back to Godhead. Because ruling over this universe is a great responsibility, Brahm\'e4
 must force many Manus in different ages to take charge of universal affairs. Under each Manu there are different kings who also execute the purpose of Lord Brahm\'e4. It is understood from previous explanations that the father of Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, King Utt\'e4nap\'e4da, ruled over the universe because his elder brother, Priyavrata, practiced austerity from the very beginning of his life. Thus up to the point of the Pracet\'e4s, the kings of the universe were all descendants of Utt\'e4nap\'e4
da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja. Since there were no suitable kings after the Pracet\'e4s, Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu went to the Gandham\'e4dana Hill to bring back his eldest son, Priyavrata, who was meditating there. Sv\'e4
yambhuva Manu requested Priyavrata to rule over the universe. When he refused, Lord Brahm\'e4 descended from the supreme planetary system, known as Satyaloka, to request Priyavrata to accept the order. Lord Brahm\'e4 d
id not come alone. He came with other great sages like Mar\'e9ci, \'c4treya and Vasi\'f1\'f6ha. To convince Priyavrata that it was necessary for him to follow the Vedic injunctions and accept the responsibility of ruling over the world, Lord Brahm\'e4
 also brought with him the personified }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  his constant associates.
\par A significant word in this verse is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sva-bhavan\'e4t,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  indicating that Lord Brahm\'e4
 descended from his own abode. Every demigod has his own abode. Indra, the King of the demigods, has his own abode, as do Candra, the lord of the moon planet, and S\'fc
rya, the predominating deity of the sun planet. There are many millions of demigods, and the stars and planets are their respective homes. This is confirmed in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Y\'e4nti deva-vrat\'e4 dev\'e4n:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "Those who worship the demigods go to their different planetar}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid856853 y systems." Lord Brahm\'e4's abode,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 the highest planetary system, is called Satyaloka or sometimes Brahmaloka. Brahmaloka usually refers to the spiritual world. The abode of Lord Brahm\'e4 is Satyaloka, but because Lord Brahm\'e4 resides there, it is also sometimes called Brahmaloka.

\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.1.8
\par }\pard\plain \s275\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13252452 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 TEXT 8
