 had finally descended from Satyaloka to Bh\'fcloka, N\'e4rada Muni, Prince Priyavrata and Sv\'e4
yambhuva Manu came forward to offer him objects of worship and to praise him in highly qualified language, according to Vedic etiquette. At that time, Lord Brahm\'e4, the original person of this universe, felt 
compassion for Priyavrata and, looking upon him with a smiling face, spoke to him as follows.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 That Lord Brahm\'e4
 descended from Satyaloka to see Priyavrata indicates that the matter was very serious. N\'e4rada Muni had come to advise Priyavrata about the value of spiritual life, knowledge, renunciation and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhakti,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and Lord Brahm\'e4 knew that N\'e4rada's instructions were very impressive. Therefore unless Lord Brahm\'e4 personally went to Gandham\'e4dana Hill to request Priyavrata, Lord Brahm\'e4 knew that prince Priya
vrata would not accept his father's order. Brahm\'e4's purpose was to break Priyavrata's determination. Therefore Brahm\'e4 first looked upon Priyavrata with compassion. His smile and compassionate features also indicated that although Brahm\'e4
 would request Priyavrata to accept household life, Priyavrata would not be out of touch with devotional service. By the blessings of a Vai\'f1\'ebava, everything is possible. This is described in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhakti-ras\'e4m\'e5
ta-sindhu}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 k\'e5p\'e4-siddhi,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or perfection attained simply by the blessings
 of a superior person. One usually becomes liberated and perfect by executing the regulative principles set down in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7\'e4stras.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 Nonetheless, many persons have achieved perfection simply by the blessings of a spiritual master or superior.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Priyavrata was the grandson of Lord Brahm\'e4
, and as joking competition sometimes takes place between grandson and grandfather, in this case also Priyavrata was determined to remain in meditation, whereas Brahm\'e4 was determined that he rule the universe. Thus Lord Brahm\'e4's af
fectionate smile and glance meant, "My dear Priyavrata, you have decided not to accept household life, but I have decided to convince you that you must accept it." Actually, Brahm\'e4
 had come to praise Priyavrata for his high standard of renunciation, austerity, penance and devotion so that he would not be deviated from devotional service, even though he would accept household life.
\par In this verse, one important word is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 s\'fckta-v\'e4kena}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (by Vedic hymns). In the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 there is the following prayer to Lord Brahm\'e4: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 hira\'ebyagarbha\'f9 samavartat\'e4gre bh\'fctasya j\'e4ta\'f9 patir eka \'e4s\'e9t.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Brahm\'e4
 was received with the appropriate Vedic hymns, and because he was welcomed according to the Vedic etiquette, he was very pleased.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.1.11
