yoga}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by power of mystic }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 yoga;}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977  }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 v\'e9rye\'eba}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by personal strength; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 man\'e9\'f1ay\'e4}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by intelligence; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 v\'e4
}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash or; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 na}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash never; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 eva}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash certainly; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 artha}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by material opulence; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 dharmai\'f9}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by the power of religion; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 parata\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by any external power; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 
svata\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by personal endeavor; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 v\'e4}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash or; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 k\'e5tam}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash the order; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 vihantum}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash to avoid; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 tanu-bh\'e5t}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash a living entity who has accepted a material body; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 vibh\'fcy\'e4t}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash is able.
\par }\pard\plain \s405\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3017748 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid2301602\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid2301602 
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 
One cannot avoid the order of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, not by the strength of severe austerities, an exalted Vedic education, or the
 power of mystic yoga, physical prowess or intellectual activities. Nor can one use his power of religion, his material opulence or any other means, either by himself or with the help of others, to defy the orders of the Supreme Lord. That is not possible
 for any living being, from Brahm\'e4 down to the ant.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Garga Upani\'f1ad,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Gargamuni says to his wife, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 etasya v\'e4 ak\'f1arasya pra\'e7\'e4sane gargi s\'fcry\'e4-candramasau vidh\'e5tau ti\'f1\'f6hata\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 My dear Garg\'e9, everything is under the control of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Even the sun, the moon and other controllers and demigods like Lord Brahm\'e4
 and King Indra are all under His control." An ordinary human being or animal who has accepted a material body cannot go beyond the jurisdiction of the Supreme Persona
lity of Godhead's control. A material body includes senses. However, the sense activities of so-called scientists who try to be free from God's law or the laws of nature are useless. This is also confirmed in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g
\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 7.14}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Mama m\'e4y\'e4 duratyay\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it i
s impossible to surpass the control of material nature, for the Supreme Personality of Godhead is working behind it. Sometimes we are proud of our austerities, penances and mystic yogic powers, but it is clearly stated herein that one cannot surpass the l
aws and directions of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, either by dint of mystic power, a scientific education, or austerities and penances. It is impossible.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 The word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 man\'e9\'f1ay\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  ("by intelligence") is of special significance. Priyavrata might argue that Lord Brahm\'e4 was requesting him to accept family life and the responsibility for ruling a kingdom, although N\'e4
rada Muni had advised him not to enter household life and be entangled in material affairs. Whom to accept would be a puzzle for Priyavrata because both Lord Brahm\'e4 and N\'e4rada Muni are authorities. Under the circumstances, the use of the word }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 man\'e9\'f1ay\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is very appropriate, for it indicates that since both N\'e4rada Muni and Lord Brahm\'e4 are authorized to give instruction, Priyavrata should neglect neither o
f them but should use his intelligence to follow the advice of both. To solve such dilemmas, \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 has given a very clear conception of intelligence. He says:
