\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 guptaye}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash for the protection; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 \'e4sth\'e4pya}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash establishing; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 svayam}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash personally; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 ati-vi\'f1ama}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash very dangerous; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 vi\'f1aya}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash material affairs; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 vi\'f1a}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash of poison; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 jala-\'e4\'e7aya}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash ocean; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 \'e4\'e7\'e4y\'e4\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash from desires; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 uparar\'e4ma}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash got relief.
\par }\pard\plain \s405\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3017748 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid2301602\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid2301602 
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu, with the assistance of Lord Brahm\'e4
, thus fulfilled his desires. With the permission of the great sage N\'e4
rada, he delivered to his son the governmental responsibility for maintaining and protecting all the planets of the universe. He thus achieved relief from the most dangerous, poisonous ocean of material desires.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Sv\'e4
yambhuva Manu was practically hopeless because such a great personality as N\'e4rada was instructing his son Priyavrata not to accept household life. Now he was very pleased that Lord Brahm\'e4
 had interfered by inducing his son to accept the responsibility for ruling the government of the universe. From }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 we get information that Vaivasvata Manu was the son of the sun-god and that his son, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Ik\'f1v\'e4ku, ruled this planet earth. Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu, however, appears to have been in charge of the entir
e universe, and he entrusted to his son, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Priyavrata, the responsibility for maintaining and protecting all the planetary systems. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Dhar\'e4-ma\'eb\'f2ala}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 means "planet." This earth, for instance, is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 dhar\'e4-ma\'eb\'f2ala.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Akhila,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  however, means "all" or "uni
versal." It is therefore difficult to understand where Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Priyavrata was situated, but from this literature his position certainly appears greater than that of Vaivasvata Manu, for he was entrusted with all the planetary systems of the entire universe.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Another significant statement is that Sv\'e4
yambhuva Manu took great satisfaction from abnegating the responsibility for ruling all the planetary systems of the universe. At present, politicians are very eager to take charge of the government, and they eng
age their men in canvassing from door to door to get votes to win the post of president or a similar exalted office. On the contrary, however, herein we find that King Priyavrata had to be persuaded by Lord Brahm\'e4
 to accept the post of emperor of the entire universe. Similarly, his father, Sv\'e4
yambhuva Manu, felt relieved to entrust the universal government to Priyavrata. Thus it is evident that the kings and executive heads of government in the Vedic age never accepted their positions for sense enjoyment. Such exalted kings, who were known as 
}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 r\'e4jar\'f1is,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  ruled only to maintain and protect the kingdom for the welfare of the citizens. The history of Priyavrata and Sv\'e4
yambhuva Manu describes how exemplary, responsible monarchs performed the duties of government with disinterest, keeping themselves always aloof from the contamination of material attachment.
\par Material affairs have herein been compared to an ocean of poison. They have been described in a similar way by \'c7r\'e9la Narottama d\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura in one of his songs:
\par }\pard\plain \s406\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14365851 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 sa\'e0s\'e4ra-vi\'f1\'e4nale,     div\'e4-ni\'e7i hiy\'e4 jvale,\line ju\'f2
\'e4ite n\'e4 kainu up\'e4ya
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "My heart is always burning in the fire of material existence}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid14365851 ,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and I have made no provisions for getting out of it."
\par }\pard\plain \s406\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14365851 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 golokera prema-dhana,     hari-n\'e4ma-sa\'eck\'e9rtana,\line rati n\'e4
 janmila kene t\'e4ya
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "The only remedy is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 hari-n\'e4ma-sa\'eck
\'e9rtana,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the chanting of the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mah\'e4-mantra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  which is imported from the spiritual world, Goloka V\'e5nd\'e4
vana. How unfortunate I am that I have no attraction for this." Manu wanted to seek shelter at the lotus feet o
f the Lord, and therefore when his son Priyavrata took charge of his worldly affairs, Manu was very relieved. That is the system of Vedic civilization. At the end of life, one must free himself from worldly affairs and completely engage in the service of 
the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 The word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 surar\'f1i-vara-anumatena}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is also significant. Manu entrusted the government to his son with the permission of the great saint N\'e4rada. This is particularly mentioned because although N\'e4rada wanted Priyavrata to become free from all material 
affairs, when Priyavrata took charge of the universe by the request of Lord Brahm\'e4 and Manu, N\'e4rada was also very pleased.
