 by accepting the duties of government, but also married Barhi\'f1mat\'e9, the daughter of Vi\'e7vakarm\'e4, one of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 praj\'e4patis.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Since Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Priyavrata was fully trained in transcendental knowledge, he could have returned home and conducted the business of government as a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahmac\'e4r\'e9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 Instead, however, when he returned to household life, he accepted a wife also. The principle is that when one becomes a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 g\'e5hastha,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  he must live perfectly in that order, wh
ich means he must live peacefully with a wife and children. When Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu's first wife died, His mother requested Him to marry for a second time. He was twenty years old and was going to take }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sanny\'e4sa}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  at the age of twenty-four, yet by the reques
t of His mother, He married. "As long as I am in household life," He told His mother, "I must have a wife, for household life does not mean staying in a house. Real household life means living in a house with a wife."
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Three words in this verse are very significant\emdash }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 u ha v\'e4va.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  These words are used to express wonder. Priyavrata Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja had taken a vow of renunciation, but accepting a wife and begetting children have nothing to do with the path of renunciation; these are activities on the path of enjoyment. It was a source of great wonder, therefore, that Priyavrata Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, who had followed the path of renunciation, had now accepted the path of enjoyment.
