\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  stage is the topmost position in renounced life. In }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sanny\'e4sa,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the renounced order, there are four stages\emdash }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ku\'f6\'e9
caka, bah\'fcdaka, parivr\'e4jak\'e4c\'e4rya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 paramaha\'e0sa.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 According to the Vedic system, when one accepts the renounced order, he stays outside his village in a cottage, and his necessities, especially his food, are supplied from home. This is called the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ku\'f6\'e9caka}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  stage. When a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sanny\'e4s\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 advances further, he no longer accepts anything from home: instead, he collects his necessities, especially his food, from many places. This system is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 m\'e4dhukar\'e9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 which literally means "the profession of the bumblebees." As bumblebees collect honey from many flowers, a little from each, so a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sanny\'e4s\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 should beg from door to door but not accept very much food from any particular house; he should collect a little bit from every house. This is called the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bah\'fcdaka}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  stage. When a }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sanny\'e4s\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is still more experienced, he travels all over the world to preach the glories of Lord V\'e4sudeva. He is then known as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 parivr\'e4jak\'e4c\'e4
rya.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sanny\'e4s\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  reaches the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 paramaha\'e0sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 stage when he finishes his preaching work and sits down in one place, strictly for the sake of advancing in spiritual life. An actual }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 paramaha\'e0sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 is one who completely controls his senses and engages in the unalloyed service of the Lord. Therefore all three of these sons of Priyavrata, namely Kavi, Mah\'e4v\'e9ra and Savana, were situated in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 paramaha\'e0sa}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  stage from the very beginning. Their senses could not disturb them, for their senses were completely engaged in serving the Lord. Therefore the three brothers are described in this verse as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
upa\'e7ama-\'e7\'e9l\'e4\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Upa\'e7ama}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  means "complete
ly subdued." Because they completely subdued their senses, they are understood to have been great sages and saints.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
