\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  that anyone neglecting it would immediately flee from his presence as soon as the King warned him by fighting or administering light punishment. Indeed, Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Priyavrata would not have to fight, for simply because of his strong determination, they dared not disobey the rules and regulations of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 It is said that unless human society is regulated by }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is no better than a bestial society of cats and dogs. Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Priyavrata, therefore, strictly maintained }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  by his extraordinary, unparalleled prowess.
