\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 ayi nanda-tanuja ki\'eckara\'e0\line patita\'e0 m\'e4\'e0 vi\'f1ame bhav\'e4\'e0
budhau\line k\'e5pay\'e4 tava p\'e4da-pa\'eckaja-\line sthita-dh\'fcl\'e9-sad\'e5\'e7a\'e0 vicintaya 
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "O son of Nanda Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, I am Your eternal servant, yet somehow or other I have fallen into the ocean of birth and death. Please pick me up from this ocean of death and place me as one of the atoms of Your lotus feet." Lord Caitanya teaches us to come in touch with the dust 
of the Lord's lotus feet, for then there will undoubtedly be all success.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Because of the material body, every living entity in material existence is always disturbed by }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sad-gu\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  six whips\emdash 
hunger, thirst, lamentation, illusion, invalidity and death. Furthermore, another }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sad-gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are the mind and five sense organs. Not to speak of a sanctified devotee, even a }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ca\'eb\'f2\'e4la,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  an outcaste, who is untouchable, is immediately freed from material bondage if he utters the holy name of the Lord even once. Sometimes caste }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  argue that unless one changes his body he cannot be accepted as a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 for since the present body is obtained as a result of past actions, one who has in the past acted as a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  takes birth in a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  family. Therefore, they contend, without such a brahminical body, one cannot be accepted as a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Herein it is said, however, that even }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vid\'fcra-vigata,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ca\'eb\'f2\'e4la}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash a fifth-class untouchable\emdash 
is freed if he utters the holy name even once. Being freed means that he immediately changes his body. San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 confirms this:
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 yath\'e4 k\'e4\'efcanat\'e4\'e0 y\'e4ti\line k\'e4\'e0sya\'e0 rasa-vidh\'e4nata
\'f9\line tath\'e4 d\'e9k\'f1\'e4-vidh\'e4nena\line dvijatva\'e0 j\'e4yate n\'e5\'eb\'e4m
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 When a person, even though a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ca\'eb\'f2
\'e4la,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is initiated by a pure devotee into chanting the holy name of the Lord, his body change
s as he follows the instructions of the spiritual master. Although one cannot see how his body has changed, we must accept, on the grounds of the authoritative statements of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7\'e4stras,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  that he changes his body. This is to be understood without arguments. This verse clearly says, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sa jah\'e4ti bandham:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 "He gives up his material bondage." The body is a symbolic representation of material bondage according to one's }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 Although sometimes we cannot see the gross body changing, chanting the holy name of the Sup
reme Lord immediately changes the subtle body, and because the subtle body changes, the living entity is immediately freed from material bondage. After all, changes of the gross body are conducted by the subtle body. After the destruction of the gross bod
y
, the subtle body takes the living entity from his present gross body to another. In the subtle body, the mind is predominant, and therefore if one's mind is always absorbed in remembering the activities or the lotus feet of the Lord, he is to be understo
od to have already changed his present body and become purified. Therefore it is irrefutable that a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ca\'eb\'f2\'e4la,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or any fallen or lowborn person, can become a }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  simply by the method of bona fide initiation.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.1.36
