ause of his mellifluous words. She enjoyed royal happiness with \'c4gn\'e9dhra for many years before returning to her abode in the heavenly planets. In her womb \'c4gn\'e9dhra begot nine sons-N\'e4bhi, Ki\'e0puru\'f1a, Harivar\'f1a, Il\'e4v\'e5
ta, Ramyaka, Hira\'ebmaya, Kuru, Bhadr\'e4\'e7va and Ketum\'e4la. He gave them nine islands with names corresponding to theirs. \'c4gn\'e9
dhra, however, his senses unsatisfied, was always thinking of his celestial wife, and therefore in his next life he was born in her celestial planet. After the death of \'c4gn\'e9dhra, his nine sons married nine daughters of Meru named Merudev\'e9, Pratir
\'fcp\'e4, Ugrada\'e0\'f1\'f6r\'e9, Lat\'e4, Ramy\'e4, \'c7y\'e4m\'e4, N\'e4r\'e9, Bhadr\'e4 and Devav\'e9ti.
