\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or desirous of being transferred to the planet named Pit\'e5loka. Pit\'e5loka is mentioned in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 y\'e4
nti deva-vrat\'e4 dev\'e4n pit\'e8n y\'e4nti pit\'e5-vrat\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). To go to this planet, one needs very good sons who can make offerings to Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and then offer the remnants to their forefathers. The purpose of the 
}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7r\'e4ddha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  ceremony is to please the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, so that after pleasing Him one may offer }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5135716\charrsid5135716 pras\'e4
da}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  to one's forefathers and in this way make them happy. The inhabitants of Pit\'e5loka are generally men of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2\'e9ya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 or fruitive activities category, who have been transferred there because of their pious activities. They can stay there as long as their descendants offer them }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vi\'f1\'ebu-}{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5135716\charrsid5135716 pras\'e4dam}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 .}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Everyone in heavenly planets such as Pit\'e5
loka, however, must return to earth after exhausting the effects of his pious acts. As confirmed in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11612319 9.21}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 k\'f1\'e9\'ebe pu\'ebye martya-loka\'e0 vi\'e7anti:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  persons who perform pious acts are transferred to higher planets, but when
 the effects of their pious acts are over, they are again transferred to earth.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Since Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Priyavrata was a great devotee, how could he have begotten a son who desired to be transferred to Pit\'e5loka? Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba says, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 pit\'e8n y\'e4nti pit\'e5-vrat\'e4\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  persons who
 desire to go to Pit\'e5loka are transferred there. Similarly, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 y\'e4nti mad-y\'e4jino 'pi m\'e4m: }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  persons who desire to be transferred to the spiritual planets, Vaiku\'eb\'f6
halokas, can also go there. Since Mah\'e4r\'e4ja \'c4gn\'e9dhra was the son of a Vai\'f1\'ebava, he should have desired to be transferred to the spiritual world, Vaiku\'eb\'f6haloka. Why, then, did he desire to be transferred to Pit\'e5
loka? In answer to this, Gosv\'e4m\'e9 Giridhara, one of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  commentators, remarks that \'c4gn\'e9dhra was born when Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Priyavrata was infatu
ated by lusty desires. This may be accepted as a fact because sons are begotten with different mentalities according to the time of their conception. According to the Vedic system, therefore, before a child is conceived, the }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 garbh\'e4dh\'e4na-sa\'e0sk\'e4ra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is perform
ed. This ceremony molds the mentality of the father in such a way that when he plants his seed in the womb of his wife, he will beget a child whose mind will be completely saturated with a devotional attitude. At the present moment, however, there are no 
such }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 garbh\'e4dh\'e4na-sa\'e0sk\'e4ras,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and therefore people generally have a lusty attitude when they beget children. Especially in this age of Kali, there are no }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 garbh\'e4dh\'e4na}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  ceremonies; everyone enjoys sex with his wife like a cat or dog. Therefore according to \'e7\'e4stric injunctions, almost all the people of this age belong to the }{
