\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 King N\'e4bhi understood that his son, \'c5\'f1
abhadeva, was very popular among the citizens and among government officers and ministers. Understanding the popularity of his son, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja N\'e4bhi enthroned Him as the emperor of 
the world to give protection to the general populace in terms of the Vedic religious system. To do this, he entrusted Him into the hands of learned br\'e4hma\'ebas, who would guide Him in administrating the government. Then Mah\'e4r\'e4ja N\'e4
bhi and his wife, Merudev\'e9, went to Badarik\'e4\'e7rama in the Himalaya Mountains, where the King engaged Himself very expertly in austerities and penances with great jubilation. In full sam\'e4
dhi he worshiped the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Nara-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, who is K\'e5\'f1\'eba in His plenary expansion. By doing so, in course of time Mah\'e4r\'e4ja N\'e4bhi was elevated to the spiritual world known as Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
