\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are significant in this verse. If work is not carried out in devotional service, it is contaminated by the modes of material nature. That is explained in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yaj\'ef\'e4rth\'e4t karma\'ebo 'nyatra loko 'ya\'e0 karma-bandhana\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 Activities performed only for the satisfaction of the Supreme Lord are pure and are not contaminated by the modes of material nature. All other activities are contaminated by the modes of ignorance and passion, as well as goodness. All material act
ivities meant for satisfying the senses are contaminated, and Mah\'e4r\'e4ja N\'e4bhi did not perform anything contaminated. He simply executed his transcendental activities even when performing }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yaj\'efa.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Consequently he obtained the Supreme Lord as his son.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.4.7
