e gratification, which is available even for dogs and hogs that eat stool. One should engage in penance and austerity to attain the divine position of devotional service. By such activity, one's heart is purified, and when one attains this position, he at
tains eternal, blissful life, which is transcendental to material happiness and which continues forever.
