\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 
As long as one does not inquire about the spiritual values of life, one is defeated and subjected to mis
eries arising from ignorance. Be it sinful or pious, karma has its resultant actions. If a person is engaged in any kind of karma, his mind is called karm\'e4
tmaka, colored with fruitive activity. As long as the mind is impure, consciousness is unclear, and as long as one is absorbed in fruitive activity, he has to accept a material body.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Generally people think that one should act very piously in order to be relieved from misery, but this is not a fact. Even though one engages in pious activity and spe
culation, he is nonetheless defeated. His only aim should be emancipation from the clutches of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 m\'e4y\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 and all material activities. Speculative knowledge and pious activity do not solve the problems of material life. One should be inquisitive to understand his spiritual position. As stated in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 4.37}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ):
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 yathaidh\'e4\'e0si samiddho 'gnir\line bhasmas\'e4t kurute 'rjuna\line j\'ef\'e4n
\'e4gni\'f9 sarva-karm\'e4\'ebi\line bhasmas\'e4t kurute tath\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"As a blazing fire turns firewood to ashes, O Arjuna, so does the fire of knowledge burn to ashes all reactions to material activities."
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Unless one understands the self and its activities, one has to be considered in material bondage. In }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid548546 (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 10.2.32}{
\cf1\insrsid548546 )}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is also said: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ye 'nye 'ravind\'e4k\'f1a vimukta-m\'e4ninas tvayy asta-bh\'e4v\'e4d avi\'e7uddha-buddhaya\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 A person who doesn't have knowledge of devotional service may think himself liberated, but actually he is not. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c4ruhya k\'e5cchre\'eba para\'e0 pada\'e0 tata\'f9 patanty adho 'n\'e4d\'e5ta-yu\'f1mad-a\'ecghraya\'f9:}
{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  such people may approach the impersonal Brahman effulgence, but they fall down again into material enjoyment because they have no knowledge of devotional service. As long as one is interested in }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4na,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  he continues enduring the miseries of material life\emdash birth, old age, disease and death. }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Karm\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  certainly take on one body after another. As far as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 are concerned, unless they are promoted to the topmost understanding, they must return to the material world. As explained in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 7.19}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ): }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bah\'fcn\'e4\'e0 janman\'e4m ante j\'ef\'e4nav\'e4n m\'e4\'e0 prapadyate.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The point is to know K\'e5\'f1\'eba, V\'e4sudeva, as everything and surrender unto Him. 
}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Karm\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  do not know this, but a devotee who is one hundred percent engaged in the devotional service of the Lord knows fully what is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4na;}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  therefore a pure devotee is no longer interested in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4na.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Any\'e4bhil\'e4\'f1it\'e4-\'e7\'fcnya\'e0 j\'ef\'e4na-karm\'e4dy-an\'e4v\'e5tam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The real }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhakta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is untouched by any tinge of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4na.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 His only purpose in life is to serve the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.5.6
