ssor unfortunately identifies with his property and wealth. Sometimes, even after renunciation, one becomes attached to a temple or to the few things that constitute the property of a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sanny\'e4s\'e9,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  but such attachment is not as strong as family attachment. The attachment to the family is the strongest illusion. In the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Satya-sa\'e0hit\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is stated:
