\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 "One who
 cannot deliver his dependents from the path of repeated birth and death should never become a spiritual master, a father, a husband, a mother or a worshipable demigod.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 There are many spiritual masters, but \'c5\'f1
abhadeva advises that one should not become a spiritual master if he is unable to save his disciple from the path of birth and death. Unless one is a pure devotee of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, he cannot save himself from the path of repeated birth and death. }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0 punar janma naiti m\'e4m eti so'rjuna.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  One ca
n stop birth and death only by returning home, back to Godhead. However, who can go back to Godhead unless he understands the Supreme Lord in truth? }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Janma karma ca me divyam eva\'e0 yo vetti tattvata\'f9.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 We have many instances in history illustrating \'c5\'f1abhadeva's instructions. 
\'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya was rejected by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja due to his inability to save Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja from the path of repeated birth and death. \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4
rya was not a pure devotee, he was more or less inclined to fruitive activity, and he objected when Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja promised to give everything to Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. Actually one is supposed to give everything to the Lord because everything belongs to the Lord. Consequently, the Supreme Lord advises in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 9.27}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ):
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 yat karo\'f1i yad a\'e7n\'e4si\line yaj juho\'f1i dad\'e4si yat\line 
yat tapasyasi kaunteya\line tat kuru\'f1va mad-arpa\'ebam
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "O son of Kunt\'e9
, all that you do, all that you eat, all that you offer and give away, as well as all austerities that you may perform, should be done as an offering unto Me." This is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhakti.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 Unless one is devoted, he cannot give everything to the Supreme Lord. Unless one can do so, he cannot become a spiritual master, husband, father or mother. Similarly, the wives of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  who were performing sacrifices gave up their relatives just to satisfy K\'e5\'f1\'eba. This is an example of a wife rejecting a husband who cannot deliver her from the impending dangers of birth and death. Similarly, Prahl\'e4
da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja rejected his father, and Bharata Mah\'e4r\'e4ja rejected his mother (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 janan\'e9 na s\'e4 sy\'e4t}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). The word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 daivam}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  indicates a demigod or one who accepts worship from a dependent. Ordinarily, the spiritual master, husband, father, mother or superior relative accepts worship from an inferior relative, but here \'c5\'f1
abhadeva forbids this. First the father, spiritual master or husband 
must be able to release the dependent from repeated birth and death. If he cannot do this, he plunges himself into the ocean of reproachment for his unlawful activities. Everyone should be very responsible and take charge of his dependents just as a spiri
tual master takes charge of his disciple or a father takes charge of his son. All these responsibilities cannot be discharged honestly unless one can save the dependent from repeated birth and death.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.5.19
