\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 My transcendental body [sac-cid-\'e4
nanda-vigraha] looks exactly like a human form, but it is not a material human body. It is inconceivable. I am not forced by nature to accept a particular type of body; I take on a body by My own sweet will. My heart is 
also spiritual, and I always think of the welfare of My devotees. Therefore within My heart can be found the process of devotional service, which is meant for the devotees. Far from My heart have I abandoned irreligion [adharma] and nondevotional activiti
es. They do not appeal to Me. Due to all these transcendental qualities, people generally pray to Me as \'c5\'f1abhadeva, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the best of all living entities.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In this verse the words }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ida\'e0 \'e7ar\'e9ra
\'e0 mama durvibh\'e4vyam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are very significant. Generally we experience two energies\emdash material energy and spiritual energy. We have some experience of t}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10954314 he material energy (earth,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  water, air, fire, ether, mind, intelligence and ego) because in the material world everyone's body is composed of
 these elements. Within the material body is the spirit soul, but we cannot see it with the material eyes. When we see a body full of spiritual energy, it is very difficult for us to understand how the spiritual energy can have a body. It is said that Lor
d \'c5\'f1abhadeva's body is completely spiritual; therefore for a materialistic person, it is very difficult to understand. For a materialistic person, the completely spiritual body is inconceivable. We have to accept the version of the }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  when our experimental perception cannot understand a subject. As stated in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9 parama\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba\'f9 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 The Supreme Lord has a body with form, but that body is not composed of material elements. It is made of spiritual bliss, eternity and l
iving force. By the inconceivable energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the Lord can appear before us in His original spiritual body, but because we have no experience of the spiritual body, we are sometimes bewildered and see the form of the Lord
 as material. The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers are completely unable to conceive of a spiritual body. They say that the spirit is always impersonal, and whenever they see something personal, they take it for granted that it is material. In }{
\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 9.11}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ) it is said:
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 avaj\'e4nanti m\'e4\'e0 m\'fc\'f2h\'e4\line m\'e4nu\'f1\'e9\'e0 tanum \'e4\'e7
ritam\line para\'e0 bh\'e4vam aj\'e4nanto\line mama bh\'fcta-mahe\'e7varam
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"Fools deride Me when I descend in the human form. They do not know My transcendental nature and My supreme dominion over all that be."
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Unintelligent people thi
nk that the Supreme Lord accepts a body composed of the material energy. We can easily understand the material body, but we cannot understand the spiritual body. Therefore \'c5\'f1abhadeva says: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ida\'e0 \'e7ar\'e9ra\'e0
 mama durvibh\'e4vyam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  In the spiritual world, everyone has a spiritual body. There is no conception of material existence there. In the spiritual world there is only service and the receiving of service. There is only }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sevya, sev\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sevaka}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash the person served, the process of service and the servant. These three 
items are completely spiritual, and therefore the spiritual world is called absolute. There is no tinge of material contamination there. Being completely transcendental to the material conception, Lord \'c5\'f1
abhadeva states that His heart is composed of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 dharma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is explained in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9
t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 18.66}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ): }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 In the spiritual world, every living entity is surrendered to the Supreme Lord and is completely on the spiritual platform. Although there are servitors, the s
erved and service, all are spiritual and variegated. At the present moment, due to our material conception}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4025764 , e}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 verything is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 durvibh\'e4vya,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  inconceivable. Being the Supreme, the Lord is called \'c5\'f1abha, the best. In terms of the Vedic language, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nityo nity\'e4n\'e4m.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  We are also spiritual}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4025764 , b}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ut we are subordinate. K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Lord, is the foremost living entity. The word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e5\'f1abha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 means "the chief," or "the supreme," and indicates the Supreme Being, or God Himself.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.5.20
