\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 Of the two energies manifest [spirit and
 dull matter], beings possessing living force [vegetables, grass, trees and plants] are superior to dull matter [stone, earth, etc.]. Superior to nonmoving plants and vegetables are worms and snakes, which can move. Superior to worms and snakes are animal
s
 that have developed intelligence. Superior to animals are human beings, and superior to human beings are ghosts because they have no material bodies. Superior to ghosts are the Gandharvas, and superior to them are the Siddhas. Superior to the Siddhas are
 the Kinnaras, and superior to them are the asuras. Superior to the asuras are the demigods, and of the demigods, Indra, the King of heaven, is supreme. Superior to Indra are the direct sons of Lord Brahm\'e4, sons like King Dak\'f1
a, and supreme among Brahm\'e4's sons is Lord \'c7iva. Since Lord \'c7iva is the son of Lord Brahm\'e4, Brahm\'e4 is considered superior, but Brahm\'e4 is also subordinate to Me, the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Because I am inclined to the br\'e4hma
\'ebas, the br\'e4hma\'ebas are best of all.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In this verse the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are given a position superior to that of the Supreme Lord. The idea is that the government should be conducted under the guidance of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Although 
\'c5\'f1abhadeva recommended His eldest son, Bharata, as emperor of the earth, he still had to follow the instructions of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 in order to govern the world perfectly. The Lord is worshiped as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahma\'ebya-deva.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The Lord is very fond of devotees, or }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  This does not refer to so-called caste }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  but to qualified }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  A }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  should be qualified with the eight qualities mentioned in text 24, such as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7ama, dama, satya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 titik\'f1\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10097791  should always be worshiped,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 and under their guidance the ruler should discharge his duty and rule the citizens. Unfortunately, in this age of Kali, the executive is not selected by very intelligent people, nor is he guided by qualified }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma
\'ebas.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Consequently, chaos results. The mass of people should be educated in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness so that according to the democratic process they can select a first-class devotee like Bharata Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja to head the government. If the head of the state is headed by qualified }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  everything is completely perfect.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In this verse, the evolutionary process is indirectly mentioned. The modern the
ory that life evolves from matter is to some extent supported in this verse because it is stated, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bh\'fcte\'f1u v\'e9rudbhya\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 That is, the living entities evolve from vegetables, grass, plants and trees, which are superior to dull matter. In other words, matter al
so has the potency to manifest living entities in the form of vegetables. In this sense, life comes out of matter, but matter also comes out of life. As K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 10.8}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 aha\'e0 sarvasya prabhavo matta\'f9 sarva\'e0 pravartate:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "I am the source o
f all spiritual and material worlds. Everything emanates from Me."
\par There are two energies\emdash material and spiritual\emdash and both originally come from K\'e5\'f1\'eba. K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the supreme living being. Although it may be said that in the material world a living force is ge
nerated from matter, it must be admitted that originally matter is generated from the supreme living being. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Nityo nity\'e4n\'e4\'e0 cetana\'e7 cetan\'e4n\'e4m.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 The conclusion is that everything, both material and spiritual, is generated from the Supreme Being. From the evolutionary point of view, perfection is reached when the living entity attains the platform of a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma
\'eba.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 A br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is a worshiper of the Supreme Brahman, and the Supreme Brahman worships the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  In other words, the devotee is subordinate to the Supreme Lord, and the Lord is inclined to see to the satisfaction of His devotee. A }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is called }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 dvija-deva,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and the Lord is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 dvija-deva-deva.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is the Lord of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas.
\par }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 The evolutionary process is also explained in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11612319 Madhya,}{\cf1\insrsid11612319  C
hapter Nineteen)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 , wherein it is said that there are two types of living entities\emdash moving and n}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10097791 onmoving. Among moving entities, there are birds, beasts,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  aquatics, h}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10097791 uman beings and so on. Of these,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the human beings are supposed to be the best, but they are few. Of these small numbers of human beings, there are many low-class human beings like }{
