 devotional service of the Lord;}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  consequently they have no material wants, nor do they possess material things. In }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11612319 Madhya}{\cf1\insrsid11612319  11.8}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu explains the position of pure Vai\'f1\'ebavas who are anxious to return home, back to Godhead. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ni\'f1
ki\'efcanasya bhagavad-bhajanonmukhasya.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Those who actually want to return back to Godhead are }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ni\'f1ki\'efcana}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash 
that is, they have no desire for material comfort. \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu advises, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sandar\'e7ana\'e0 vi\'f1ayin\'e4m atha yo\'f1it\'e4\'e0 ca h\'e4 hanta hanta visa-bhak\'f1a\'ebato 'py as\'e4dhu:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  material opulence and sense gratification through the association of women are more dangerous than poison. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  who are pure Vai\'f1\'eb
avas always engage in the Lord's service and are devoid of any desire for material gain. The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  do not worship demigods like Lord Brahm\'e4, Indra or Lord \'c7iva for 
any material comfort. They do not even ask the Supreme Lord for material profit; therefore it is concluded that the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are the supreme living entities of this world. \'c7r\'e9
 Kapiladeva also confirms this in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (3.29.33)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 :
