\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 My dear sons, you should not envy any living entity\emdash 
be he moving or nonmoving. Knowing that I am situated in them, you should offer respect to all of them at every moment. In this way, you offer respect to Me.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In this verse the word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vivikta-d\'e5gbhi\'f9
,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  meaning without envy, is used. All living entities are the abode of the Supreme Personality of Godhead in His Param\'e4tm\'e4 feature. As confirmed in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 a\'eb\'f2\'e4ntara-stha\'e0 param\'e4\'ebu-cay\'e4ntara-stham.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The Lord is situated in this universe as Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu and K\'f1\'e9rodaka\'e7
\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu. He is also situated within every atom. According to the Vedic statement: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e9\'e7\'e4v\'e4syam ida\'e0 sarvam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The Supreme Lord is situated everywhere, a
nd wherever He is situated is His temple. We even offer respects to a temple from a distant place, and all living entities should similarly be offered respect. This is different from the theory of pantheism, which holds that everything is God. Everything 
has a relationship with God because God is situated everywhere. We should not make any particular distinction between the poor and the rich like the foolish worshipers of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 daridra-n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba is present in the rich as well as the poor. One should not simply think N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba is situated among the poor. He is everywhere. An advanced devotee will offer respects to everyone\emdash 
even to cats and dogs.
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 vidy\'e4-vinaya-sampanne\line br\'e4hma\'ebe gavi hastini\line \'e7uni caiva \'e7
va-p\'e4ke ca\line pa\'eb\'f2it\'e4\'f9 sama-dar\'e7ina\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "The humble sage, by vi
rtue of true knowledge, sees with equal vision a learned and gentle }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  a cow, an elephant, a dog and a dog-eater [outcaste]." }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (Bg. 5.18)}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  This }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sama-dar\'e7ina\'f9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  equal vision, should not be mistaken to mean that the individual is the same as the Supreme 
Lord. They are always distinct. Every individual person is different from the Supreme Lord. It is a mistake to equate the individual living entity with the Supreme Lord on the plea of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vivikta-d\'e5k, sama-d\'e5k.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The Lord is always in an exalted position, even though He agrees to live everywhere. \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya, }{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid12876024 quoting}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Padma Pur\'e4\'eb
a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  states: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vivikta-d\'e5\'f1\'f6i j\'e9v\'e4n\'e4\'e0 dhi\'f1\'ebyatay\'e4 parame\'e7varasya bheda-d\'e5\'f1\'f6i\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 "One who has clear vision and who is devoid of envy can see that the Supreme Lord is separate from all living entities, although He is situated in every living entity." Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya further quotes from }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Padma Pur
\'e4\'eba:
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 upap\'e4dayet par\'e4tm\'e4na\'e0\line j\'e9vebhyo ya\'f9 pade pade\line 
bhedenaiva na caitasm\'e4t\line priyo vi\'f1\'ebos tu ka\'e7cana
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "One who sees the living entity and the Supreme Lord as 
always distinct is very dear to the Lord." }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Padma Pur\'e4\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  also states, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yo hare\'e7 caiva j\'e9v\'e4n\'e4\'e0 bheda-vakt\'e4 hare\'f9 priya\'f9:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "One who preaches that the living entities are separate from the Supreme Lord is very dear to Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu."
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.5.27
