\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11612319 Madhya}{\cf1\insrsid11612319  19.149}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ) it is said:
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-bhakta\emdash ni\'f1k\'e4ma, ataeva '\'e7\'e4nta'\line 
bhukti-mukti-siddhi-k\'e4m\'e9\emdash sakali 'a\'e7\'e4nta'
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 The word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7\'e4nta}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  means completely peaceful. Unless all one's desires are fulfilled, one cannot be peaceful. Everyone is trying to fulfill his aspirations and desires, be they material or spiritual. Those in the material world are }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 a\'e7\'e4nta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (without peace) because they have so many desires to fulfill. The pure devotee, however, is without desire. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Any\'e4bhil\'e4\'f1it\'e4-\'e7\'fc
nya:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  a pure devotee is completely free from all kinds of material desire. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Karm\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 on the other hand, are simply full of desires because they try to enjoy sense gratification. They are not peaceful in this life, nor the next, during the past, present or future. Similarly, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are always aspiring after liberation and trying to become one with the Supreme. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Yog\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are aspiring after many }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 siddhis}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (powers)\emdash }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 a\'ebim\'e4, laghim\'e4, pr\'e4pti,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  etc. However, a devotee is not at all interested in these things because he is fully dependent on the mercy of K
\'e5\'f1\'eba. K\'e5\'f1\'eba is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yoge\'e7vara,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the possessor of all mystic powers (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 siddhis}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), and He is }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e4tm\'e4r\'e4ma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  fully self-satisfied. The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yoga-siddhis}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are described in this verse. One can fly in outer space without 
the aid of a machine, and he can travel at the speed of mind. This means that as soon as a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yog\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 desires to go somewhere within this universe or even beyond this universe, he can do so immediately. One cannot estimate the speed of mind, for within a second the mind can go many millions of miles. Sometimes }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yog\'e9s
}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  enter into the bodies of other people and act as they desire when their bodies are not working properly. When the body becomes old, a perfect }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yog\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 can find a young, able body. Giving up his old body, the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yog\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  can enter into the young body and act as he pleases. Being a plenary expansion of Lord V\'e4sudeva, Lord \'c5\'f1
abhadeva possessed all these mystic }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  powers, but He was satisfied with His devotional love of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, which was evinced by the ecstatic symp
toms, such as crying, laughing and shivering.
\par }\pard\plain \s277\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Thus end the Bhaktivedanta purports of the Fifth Canto, Fifth Chapter of the }
{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  entitled "Lord \'c5\'f1abhadeva's Teachings to His Sons."
\par }\pard\plain \s20\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs20\cf19\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.6: The Activities of Lord \'c5\'f1abhadeva
\par }\pard\plain \s402\qc \li0\ri0\sb540\sa540\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0\pararsid4540608 \shading10000\cfpat10 
