 "Gaining this, one thinks there is no greater gain." When one attains the service of the Lord, which is non-different from the Lord, one does not desire anything material. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Mukti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 means relief from material existence. Bilvama\'ecgala \'d6h\'e4kura says: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mukti\'f9 mukulit\'e4\'efjali\'f9 sevate 'sm\'e4n.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  For a devotee, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mukti}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is not a very great achievement. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Mukti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 means being situated in one's constitutional position. The constitutional position of every living being is that of the Lord's servant; therefore when a living entity is engaged in the Lord's loving service, he has already attained }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mukti.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Consequently a devotee does not aspire for }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mukti,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  even if it is offered by the Supreme Lord Himself.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.6.18
