\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf9\insrsid11612319 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: }{\fs28\insrsid11612319 
My dear King, the Supreme Person, Mukunda, is actually the maintainer of all the members of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2
ava and Yadu dynasties. He is your spiritual master, worshipable Deity, friend, and the director of your activities. To say nothing of this, He sometimes serves your family as a messenger or servant. This means He worked just as ordinary servants 
do. Those engaged in getting the Lord's favor attain liberation from the Lord very easily, but He does not very easily give the opportunity to render direct service unto Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 While instructing Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 thought it wise to encourage the King because the King might be thinking of the glorious position of various royal dynasties. Especially glorious is the dynasty of Priyavrata, in which the Supreme Lord \'c5\'f1
abhadeva incarnated. Similarly, the family of Utt\'e4nap\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, the father of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Dhruva, is also glorious due to King P\'e5thu's taking birth in it. The dynasty of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Raghu is glorified because Lord R\'e4
macandra appeared in that family. As far as the Yadu and Kuru dynasties are concerned, they existed simultaneously, but of the two, the Yadu dynasty was more glorious due to the appearance of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1
it might have been thinking that the Kuru dynasty was not as fortunate as the others because the Supreme Lord did not appear in that family, neither as K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Lord R\'e4macandra, Lord \'c5\'f1abhadeva or Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu. Therefore Par\'e9
k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was encouraged by \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 in this particular verse.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
The Kuru dynasty may be considered more glorious due to the presence of devotees like the five P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas, who rendered unalloyed devotional service. Although Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba did not appear in the Kuru dynasty. He was so obligated to the P\'e4
\'eb\'f2avas' devotional service that He acted as a maintainer of the family and spiritual master of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas. Although He took birth in the Yadu dynasty, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba was more affectionate to the P\'e4\'eb\'f2
avas. By His actions, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba proved that He was more inclined to the Kuru dynasty than the Yadu dynasty. Indeed, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, indebted to the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas' devotional service, sometimes acte
d as their messenger, and He guided them through many dangerous situations. Therefore Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it should not have been saddened because Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a did not appear in his family. The Supreme Personality of Godhead is always inclined toward His pure devotees, and by His action it is clear that liberation is not very important for the devotees. Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a easily gives one liberation, but He does not so easily give one the facility to become a devotee. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Mukti\'e0 dad\'e4ti karhicit sma na bhakti-yogam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Directly o
r indirectly, it is proved that }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhakti-yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is the basis for the supreme relationship with the Supreme Lord. It is far superior to liberation. For a pure devotee of the Lord, }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mukti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is automatically attained.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.6.19
\par }\pard\plain \s275\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13252452 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 TEXT 19
