\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash due to being always conscious of His real identity; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 nija-l\'e4bha-niv\'e5tta-t\'e5\'f1\'eba\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash 
who was complete in Himself and had no other desire to fulfill; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 \'e7reyasi}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash in life's genuine welfare; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 a-tat-racanay
\'e4}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by expanding activities in the material field, mistaking the body for the self; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 cira}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash 
for a long time; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 supta}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash sleeping; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 buddhe\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash 
whose intelligence; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 lokasya}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash of men; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 ya\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash who (Lord \'c5\'f1
abhadeva); }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 karu\'ebay\'e4}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash by His causeless mercy; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 abhayam}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash 
fearlessness; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 \'e4tma-lokam}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash the real identity of the self; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 \'e4khy\'e4t}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash instructed; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 nama\'f9}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash respectful obeisances; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 bhagavate}{
\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash unto the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 \'e5\'f1abh\'e4ya}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash unto Lord \'c5\'f1abhadeva; }{
\cs410\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid4273542 tasmai}{\cs409\fs28\insrsid11612319\charrsid12079977 \emdash unto Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord \'c5\'f1
abhadeva, was fully aware o
f His true identity; therefore He was self-sufficient, and He did not desire external gratification. There was no need for Him to aspire for success, since He was complete in Himself. Those who unnecessarily engage in bodily conceptions and create an atmo
sphere of materialism are always ignorant of their real self-interest. Out of His causeless mercy, Lord \'c5\'f1
abhadeva taught the self's real identity and the goal of life. We therefore offer our respectful obeisances unto the Lord, who appeared as Lord \'c5\'f1abhadeva.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 This is the summary of this chapter, in which the activities of Lord \'c5\'f1
abhadeva are described. Being the Supreme Personality of Godhead Himself, Lord \'c5\'f1abhadeva is complete in Himself. We living entities, as parts and parcels of the Supreme Lord, should follow the instructions of Lord \'c5\'f1
abhadeva and become self-sufficient. We should not create unnecessary demands due to the bodily conception. When one is self-realized, he is sufficiently satisfied due to being situated in his original spiritual position. As confirmed in }{
\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 18.54}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ): }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Brahma-bh\'fcta\'f9 prasann\'e4tm\'e4 na \'e7ocati na k\'e4\'eck\'f1ati.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  This is the goal of all living entities. Even though one may be situated within this material world, he can become fully satisfied and devoid of hankering an
d lamentation simply by following the instructions of the Lord as set forth in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Satisfaction through self-realization is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 svar\'fcp\'e4nanda.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The conditioned soul, eternally sleeping in darkness, does not understand his s
elf-interest. He simply tries to become happy by making material adjustments, but this is impossible. It is therefore said in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam, na te vidu\'f9 sv\'e4rtha-gati\'e0 hi vi\'f1\'ebum:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  due to gross ignorance, the conditioned soul does not know that his real self-interest is to take shelter at the lotus feet of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. To try to become happy by adjusting the material atmosphere is a useless endeavor. Indeed, it is impossible. By His personal behavior and instructions, Lord \'c5\'f1abhadeva enlightened the conditi
oned soul and showed him how to become self-sufficient in his spiritual identity.
\par }\pard\plain \s277\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Thus end the Bhaktivedanta purports of the Fifth Canto, Sixth Chapter, of the 
}{\cs341\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  entitled "The Activities of Lord \'c5\'f1abhadeva."
\par }\pard\plain \s20\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs20\cf19\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.7: The Activities of King Bharata
\par }\pard\plain \s402\qc \li0\ri0\sb540\sa540\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0\pararsid4540608 \shading10000\cfpat10 
\b\f35\fs36\cf8\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid7416444 CHAPTER SEVEN}{\insrsid3693039 \line }{\insrsid11612319 The Activities of King Bharata
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10425876 \v\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid10425876\charrsid10425876 In this chapter, the activities of King Bharata Mah\'e4r\'e4
