\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 After performing the preliminaries of various sacrifices, Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja Bharata offered the results in the name of religion to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, V\'e4sudeva. In other words, he performed all the yaj\'efas for the satisfaction of Lord V\'e4sudeva, K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Bharata thought that since the demigods were different parts of V\'e4sudeva's body, He controls those who are explained in the Vedic mantras. By thinking in this way, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bharata was freed from all material contaminat
ion, such as attachment, lust and greed. When the priests were about to offer the sacrificial ingredients into the fire, Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Bharata expertly understood how the offering made to different demigods was simply an offering to the different limbs of the Lord. For instance, Indra is the arm of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and S\'fcrya [the sun] is His eye. Thus Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja Bharata considered that the oblations offered to different demigods were actually offered unto the different limbs of Lord V\'e4sudeva.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
The Supreme Personality of Godhead says that as long as one does not develop the pure devotional service of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7rava\'eba\'e0 k\'e9rtanam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 hearing and chanting, one must carry out his prescribed duties. Since Bharata Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was a great devotee, one may ask why he performed so many sacrifices that are actually meant for }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karm\'e9s.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The fact is that he was simply following the orders of V\'e4sudeva. As K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sarva dharm
\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "Abandon all varieties of religion and just surrender unto Me." (}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5923948 Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 18.66}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
) Whatever we do, we should constantly remember V\'e4sudeva. People are generally addicted to offering obeisances to various demigods, but Bharata Mah\'e4r\'e4ja simply wanted to please Lord V\'e4sudeva. As stated in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhokt\'e4ra\'e0 yaj\'efa-tapas\'e4\'e0 sarva-loka-mahe\'e7varam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5923948 Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 5.29}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). A }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yaj\'efa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  may be carried out to satisfy a particular demigod, but when the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yaj\'efa is}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 offered to the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yaj\'efa-puru\'f1a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, the demigods are satisfied. The purpose of performing different }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yaj\'efas}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is to sat
isfy the Supreme Lord. One may perform them in the name of different demigods or directly. If we directly offer oblations to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the demigods are automatically satisfied. If we water the root of a tree, the branches, twigs,
 
fruits and flowers are automatically satisfied. When one offers sacrifices to different demigods, one should remember that the demigods are simply parts of the body of the Supreme. If we worship the hand of a person, we intend to satisfy the person himsel
f
. If we massage a person's legs, we do not really serve the legs but the person who possesses the legs. All the demigods are different parts of the Lord, and if we offer service to them, we actually serve the Lord Himself. Demigod worship is mentioned in 
}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4, }{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid5923948 but}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  actually the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7lokas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 advocate worship of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Govinda. For instance, worship of the goddess Durg\'e4 is mentioned this way in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (5.44)}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 :
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 s\'e5\'f1\'f6i-sthiti-pralaya-s\'e4dhana-\'e7aktir ek\'e4\line ch\'e4
yeva yasya bhuvan\'e4ni vibharti durg\'e4\line icch\'e4nur\'fcpam api yasya ca ce\'f1\'f6ate s\'e4\line govindam \'e4di-puru\'f1a\'e0 tam aha\'e0 bhaj\'e4mi
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Following the orders of \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the goddess Durg\'e4
 creates, maintains and annihilates. \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba also confirms this statement in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 May\'e4dhyak\'f1e\'eba prak\'e5ti\'f9 s
\'fcyate sa-car\'e4caram:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "This material nature is working under My direction, O son of Kunt\'e9, and it is producing all moving and unmoving beings." (}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5923948 Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 9.10}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 )
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 We should worship the demigods in that spirit. Because the goddess Durg\'e4
 satisfies K\'e5\'f1\'eba, we should therefore offer respects to goddess Durg\'e4. Because Lord \'c7iva is nothing but K\'e5\'f1\'eba's functional body, we should therefore offer respects to Lord \'c7iva. Similarly, we should offer respects to Brahm\'e4
, Agni and S\'fcrya. There are many offerings to different demigods, and one should always remember that these offerings are usually meant to satisfy the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Bharata Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja did not aspire to receive some benediction from demigods. His aim was to please the Supreme Lord. In the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Mah\'e4bh\'e4rata,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  among the thousand names of Vi\'f1\'ebu, it is said }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yaj\'efa-bhug yaj\'efa-k\'e5d yaj\'efa\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid13851462 The}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  enjoyer of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yaj\'efa, }{
\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid13851462 the}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  performer of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yaj\'efa and yaj\'efa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 itself are the Supreme Lord. The Supreme Lord is the performer of everything, but out of ignorance the living entity thinks that he is the actor. As long as we think we are the actors, we bring about }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma-bandha}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (bondage to activity). If we act for }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yaj\'efa,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  for K\'e5\'f1\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4025764 , t}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 here is no }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma-bandha.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Yaj\'ef\'e4rth\'e4t karma\'ebo 'nyatra loko 'ya\'e0 karma-bandhana\'f9:}{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 "Work done as a sacrifice for Vi\'f1\'ebu has to be performed}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4025764 , o}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 therwise work binds one to this material world." }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid548546 (}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid13851462 Bg.}{
\cs337\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 3.9}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid548546 )}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11612319 
\par }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Following the instructions of Bharata Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, we should act not for our personal satisfaction but for the satisfaction of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. In }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 17.28}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ) it is also stated:
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 a\'e7raddhay\'e4 huta\'e0 datta\'e0\line tapas tapta\'e0 k\'e5ta\'e0 ca yat\line 
asad ity ucyate p\'e4rtha\line na ca tat pretya no iha
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Sacrifices, austerities and charities performed without faith in the Supreme Personality of Godhead are nonpermanent. Regardless of whatever rituals are performed, they are called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 asat,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 nonpermanent. They are therefore useless both in this life and the next.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Kings like Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Ambar\'e9\'f1a and many other }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 r\'e4jar\'f1is}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  who were pure devotees of the Lord simply passed their time in the
 service of the Supreme Lord. When a pure devotee executes some service through the agency of another person, he should not be criticized, for his activities are meant for the satisfaction of the Supreme Lord. A devotee may have a priest perform some }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and the priest may not be a pure Vai\'f1\'ebava, but because the devotee wants to please the Supreme Lord, he should not be criticized. The word }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ap\'fcrva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is very significant. The resultant actions of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ap\'fcrva.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  When we act piously or impiously, immediate results do not ensue. We therefore wait for the results, which are called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ap\'fcrva.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 The results are manifest in the future. Even the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sm\'e4rtas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  accept this }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ap\'fcrva.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 Pure devotees simply act for the pleasure of the Supreme Personality of Godhead; therefore the results of their activities are spiritual, or permanent. They are not like those of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karm\'e9s,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  which are nonpermanent. This is confirmed in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 4.23}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ):
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 gata-sa\'ecgasya muktasya\line j\'ef\'e4n\'e4vasthita-cetasa\'f9\line yaj\'ef\'e4y
\'e4carata\'f9 karma\line samagra\'e0 pravil\'e9yate
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"The work of a man who is unattached to the modes of material nature and who is fully situated in transcendental knowledge merges entirely into transcendence."
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
A devotee is always free from material contamination. He is fully situated in knowledge, and therefore his sacrifices are intended for the satisfaction of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
