\cs337\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid11741223 Bg.}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 14.26}{\cf1\insrsid548546 )}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  To remain immune from the material qualities, one must engage himself in devotional service\emdash 
}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7rava\'eba\'e0 k\'e9rtana\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  That is the perfection of life. When Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bharata took birth as a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  he was not very interested in the duties of a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  but within he remained a pure Vai\'f1\'eb
ava, always thinking of the lotus feet of the Lord. As advised in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 man-man\'e4 bhava mad-bhakto mad-y\'e4j\'e9 m\'e4\'e0 namaskuru.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  This is the only process by which one can be saved from the danger of repeated birth and death.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.9.4
