\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 The br\'e4hma\'eba father of Ja\'f2
a Bharata considered his son his heart and soul, and therefore he was very much attached to him. He thought it wise to educate his son properly, and being absorbed in this unsuccessful endeavor, he tried to teac
h his son the rules and regulations of brahmacarya\emdash 
including the execution of the Vedic vows, cleanliness, study of the Vedas, the regulative methods, service to the spiritual master and the method of offering a fire sacrifice. He tried his best to teach h
is son in this way, but all his endeavors failed. In his heart he hoped that his son would be a learned scholar, but all his attempts were unsuccessful. Like everyone, this br\'e4hma\'eb
a was attached to his home, and he had forgotten that someday he would die. Death, however, was not forgetful. At the proper time, death appeared and took him away.
\par }\pard\plain \s442\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7300536 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Those too attached to family life, who forget that death comes in the future to take them away, become attached and unable to finish their duty as human beings
. The duty of human life is to solve all the problems of life, but instead people remain attached to family affairs and duties. Although they forget death, death will not forget them. Suddenly they will be kicked off the platform of a peaceful family life
. One may forget that he has to die, but death never forgets. Death comes always at the right time. The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  father of Ja\'f2a Bharata wanted to teach his son the process of }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahmacarya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  but he was unsuccessful due to his son's unwillingness to undergo the process of Vedic advancement. Ja\'f2
a Bharata was simply concerned with returning home, back to Godhead, by executing devotional service through }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7rava\'eba\'e0 k\'e9rtana\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 He did not care for the Vedic instructions of his father. When one is fully interested in the service of the Lord, he does not need to follow all the regulative principles enunciated in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Of course, for an ordinary man, the Vedic principles are imperative. No one can avoid them. But when one has attained the perfection of devotional service, it is not very important to follow the Vedic principles. Lord K\'e5\'f1
\'eba advised Arjuna to ascend to the platform of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nistraigu\'ebya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the transcendental position above the Vedic principles.
\par }\pard\plain \s427\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13190186 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 traigu\'ebya-vi\'f1ay\'e4 ved\'e4\line nistraigu\'ebyo bhav\'e4rjuna\line 
nirdvandvo nitya-sattva-stho\line niryoga-k\'f1ema \'e4tmav\'e4n
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 mainly deal with the subject of the three modes of material nature. Rise above these modes, O Arjuna. Be transcendental to all of them. Be free from all dualities and from all anxieties for gain and safety, and be established in the Self." }{
\cf1\insrsid11612319 (Bg. 2.45)
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.9.7
