a Bharata, was successfully accepted by King Rah\'fcga\'eba, ruler of the states known as Sindhu and Sauv\'e9ra. The King forced Ja\'f2a Bharata to carry his palanquin and chastised him because he did not carry it properly. A carrier of King Rah\'fcga\'eb
a's palanquin was needed, and to fulfill this need the chief carriers found Ja\'f2a Bharata as the most likely person to do the work. He was therefore forced to carry the palanquin. Ja\'f2
a Bharata, however, did not protest this proud order, but humbly accepted the job and carried the palanquin. While carrying it, however, he was very careful to see that he did not step on an ant, and whenever he saw one, he would stop until the ant
