\fs28\insrsid11612319  My dear King, after this, King Rah\'fcga\'eba, ruler of the states known as Sindhu and Sauv\'e9ra, was going to Kapil\'e4\'e7rama. When the King's chief palanquin carriers reached the banks of the River Ik\'f1umat\'e9
, they needed another carrier. Therefore they began searching for someone, and by chance they came upon Ja\'f2a Bharata. They considered the fact that Ja\'f2
a Bharata was very young and strong and had firm limbs. Like cows and asses, he was quite fit to carry loads. Thinking in this way, although the great soul Ja\'f2a Bharata was unfit for such work, they nonetheless unhesitatingly forc
ed him to carry the palanquin.
