a Bharata was completely liberated. He did not even care when the dacoits attempted to kill his body; he knew that he certainly was not the body. Even if the body were killed, he would not have cared, for he was th
oroughly convinced of the proposition found in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 2.20}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ): }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 na hanyate hanyam\'e4ne \'e7
ar\'e9re.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He knew that he could not be killed even if his body were killed. Although he did not protest, the Supreme Personality of Godhead in His agent could not toler
ate the injustice of the dacoits; therefore he was saved by the mercy of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, and the dacoits were killed. In this case, while carrying the palanquin, he also knew that he was not the body. This body was very strong and stout, in sound condition and quit
e competent to carry the palanquin. Due to his being freed from the bodily conception, the sarcastic words of the King did not at all affect him. The body is created according to one's }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 and material nature supplies the ingredients for the development
 of a certain type of body. The soul the body covers is different from the bodily construction; therefore anything favorable or mischievous done to the body does not affect the spirit soul. The Vedic injunction is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 asa
\'ecgo hy aya\'e0 puru\'f1a\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the spirit soul is always unaffected by material arrangements.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.10.7
