aratha ruled Ayodhy\'e4, the great sage Vi\'e7v\'e4mitra once came to him to take away Lord R\'e4macandra and Lak\'f1ma\'eba to the forest to kill a demon. When the saintly person Vi\'e7v\'e4mitra came to the court of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Da\'e7
aratha, the King, in order to receive the saintly person, asked him, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 aihi\'f1\'f6a\'e0 yat tat punar janma jay\'e4ya.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 He asked the sage whether everything was going on well in his endeavor to conquer the repetition of birth and death. The whole process of Vedic civilization is based on this point. We must know how to conquer the repetition of birth and death. Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja Rah\'fcga\'eba also knew the purpose of life; therefore when Ja\'f2a Bharata put the philosophy of life before him, he immediately appreciated it. This is the foundation of Vedic society. Learned scholars, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4
hma\'ebas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  saintly persons and sages who were fully aware of the Vedic purpose advised the royal order how to benefit the general masses, and by their cooperation, the general masses were bene
fited. Therefore everything was successful. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Rah\'fcga\'eba attained this perfection of understanding the value of human life; therefore he regretted his insulting words to Ja\'f2
a Bharata, and he immediately descended from his palanquin and fell down at the lotus feet of Ja\'f2a Bharata in order to be excused and to hear from him further about the values of life known as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahma jij\'ef\'e4s\'e4
}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (inquiry into the Absolute Truth). At the present moment, high government officials are ignorant of the values of life, and wh
en saintly persons endeavor to broadcast the Vedic knowledge, the so-called executives do not offer their respectful obeisances but try to obstruct the spiritual propaganda. Thus one can say that the former kingly government was like heaven and that the p
resent government is like hell.
