\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  which recommend various fruitive activities for elevation to heavenly planets, resultant good birth, p
ower and so forth. Being desirous of sense gratification and opulent life, they say there is nothing more than this." }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid15875778 Bg.}{\cf1\insrsid11612319  2.42-43)
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 veda-v\'e4da}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 followers of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are generally inclined to }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the performance of sacrifice according to the Ve
dic injunctions. They are thereby promoted to higher planetary systems. They generally practice the C\'e4turm\'e4sya system. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ak\'f1ayya\'e0 ha vai c\'e4turm\'e4sya-y\'e4jina\'f9 suk\'e5ta\'e0 bhavati:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  one who performs the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 c\'e4turm\'e4sya-yaj\'efa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  becomes pious. By becoming pious, one may be promoted to the higher planetary systems (}{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'fcrdhva\'e0 gacchanti sattva-sth\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). Some of the followers of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are attached to }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the fruitive activities of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 in order to be promoted to a higher standard of life. Others argue that this is not the purpose of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Tad yathaiveha karma jita\'f9 loka\'f9 k\'f1
\'e9yate evam evam utra pu\'ebya jita\'f9 loka\'f9 k\'f1\'e9yate.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  In this world someone may become very highly elevated by taking birth in an aristocratic family, by being well educated, beautiful or very rich.
 These are the gifts for pious activities enacted in the past life. However, these will be finished when the stock of pious activity is finished. If we become attached to pious activities, we may get these various worldly facilities in the next life and m
ay take birth in the heavenly planets. But all this will eventually be finished. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 K\'f1\'e9\'ebe pu\'ebye martya-loka\'e0 vi\'e7anti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (Bg. }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11612319 9.21}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ): when the stock of pious activity is finished, one again has to come to this }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 martya-loka.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  According to the Vedic injunctions, the pe
rformance of pious activity is not really the objective of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The objective of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is explained in }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedai\'e7 ca sarvair aham eva vedya\'f9:}{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 the objective of the }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is to understand K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Those who are }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 veda-v\'e4d\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 are not actually advanced in knowledge, and those who are followers of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (Brahman understanding) are also not perfect. However, when one comes to the platform of }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 up\'e4san\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and accepts the worship of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he becomes perfect (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e4r\'e4dhan\'e4n\'e4\'e0 sarve\'f1\'e4\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebor 
\'e4r\'e4dhana\'e0 param}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). In the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 the worship of different demigods and the performance of sacrifice are certainly, mentioned, but such worship is inferior because the worshipers do not know that the ultimate goal is Vi\'f1\'ebu (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 na te vidu\'f9 sv\'e4
rtha-gati\'e0 hi vi\'f1\'ebum}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). When one comes to the platform of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vi\'f1\'ebor \'e4r\'e4dhanam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhakti-yoga,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  one has attained the perfection of life. Otherwise, as indicated in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  one is not a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 tattva-v\'e4d\'e9}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  but a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 veda-v\'e4d\'e9, a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  blind follower of the Vedic injunctions. A }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 veda-v\'e4d\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 cannot be purified from material contamination unless he becomes a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 tattva-v\'e4d\'e9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  that is, one who knows }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 tattva,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 the Absolute Truth. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Tattva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is also experienced in three features}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid12130215 \emdash }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahmeti param\'e4tmeti bhagav\'e4n iti \'e7abdyate.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Even after coming to the platform of understanding }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 tattva,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  one must worship Bhagav\'e4n, Vi\'f1\'ebu and His expansions, or one is not yet perfect. }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bah\'fcn\'e4\'e0 janman\'e4m ante j\'ef\'e4nav\'e4n m\'e4\'e0 prapadyate:}{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 after many births, one who is actually in knowledge surrenders unto K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. The conclusion is that unintelligent men with a poor fund of knowledge cannot understand Bhagav\'e4n, Brahman or Param\'e4tm\'e4, but after studying the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 and attaining the understanding of the Absolute Truth, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, one is supposed to be on the platform of perfect knowledge.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.11.3
