\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 
A dream becomes automatically known to a person as false and immaterial, and similarly one eventually realizes that material happiness in this life or the next, on this planet or a higher planet, is insignificant.
 When one realizes this, the Vedas, although an excellent source, are insufficient to bring about direct knowledge of the truth.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11027688 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 2.45}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), K\'e5\'f1\'eba advised Arjuna to become transcendental to the material activities impelled by the three material modes of nature (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
traigu\'ebya-vi\'f1ay\'e4 ved\'e4 nistraigu\'ebyo bhav\'e4rjuna}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
). The purpose of Vedic study is to transcend the activities of the three modes of material nature. Of course in the material world the mode of goodness is accepted as the best, and one can be promoted to the higher planetary systems by being on the }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sattva-gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  platform. However, that is not perfection. One must come to the conclusion that even the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sattva-gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 platform is also not good. One may dream that he has become a king with a goo
d family, wife and children, but immediately at the end of that dream he comes to the conclusion that it is false. Similarly, all kinds of material happiness are undesirable for a person who wants spiritual salvation. If a person does not come to the conc
lusion that he has nothing to do with any kind of material happiness, he cannot come to the platform of understanding the Absolute Truth, or }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 tattva j\'ef\'e4na.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Karm\'e9s, j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yog\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are after some material elevation. The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karm\'e9s}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  work hard day and night for some bodily comfort, and the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  simply speculate about how to get out of the entanglement of }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and merge into the Brahman effulgence. The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yog\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 are very much addicted to the acquisition of material perfection and magical powers. All of them are trying to be materially perfect, but a devotee very easily comes to the platform of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nirgu\'eba}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  in devotional service, and consequently for the devotee the results of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma, j\'ef\'e4na and yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 become very insignificant. Therefore only the devotee is on the platform of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 tattva j\'ef\'e4na,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  not the others. Of course the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9's}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  position is better than that of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karm\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  but that position is also insufficient. The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9 must}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  actually become liberated, and after liberation he may be situated in devotional service (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mad-bhakti\'e0 labhate par\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.11.4
