the individual soul; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 et\'e4\'f9}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash all these; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 manasa\'f9}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash of the mind; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 vibh\'fct\'e9\'f9}{\insrsid11612319 
\emdash different activities; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 j\'e9vasya}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash of the living entity; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 m\'e4y\'e4-racitasya}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash created by the external, material energy; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 nity\'e4\'f9}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash from time immemorial; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 \'e4virhit\'e4\'f9}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash sometimes manifested; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 kv\'e4pi}{\insrsid11612319 
\emdash somewhere; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 tirohit\'e4\'f9 ca}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash and not manifested; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 \'e7uddha\'f9}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash purified; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 vica\'f1\'f6e}{
\insrsid11612319 \emdash sees this; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 hi}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash certainly; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 avi\'e7uddha}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash unpurified; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 kartu\'f9}{\insrsid11612319 
\emdash of the doer.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11027688 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 The individual soul bereft of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness has many ideas and activities created in the mind by the external energy. They have been existing from time immemorial. Sometimes they are manifest in the wakening state and in the dream state, but during deep sleep }{
\fs28\insrsid15161683 [}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 unconsciousness] or trance, they disappear. A person who is liberated in this life }{\fs28\insrsid15161683 [}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 j\'e9van-mukta] can see all these things vividly.
\par }\pard\plain \s440\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9665590 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319\charrsid16721030 PURPORT}{\insrsid11612319 
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 As stated in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 13.3}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid16721030 k\'f1etra}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'efa\'e0 c\'e4pi m\'e4\'e0 viddhi sarva-k\'f1etre\'f1u bh\'e4rata.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  There are two kinds of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 k\'f1etraj\'efa,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 or living beings. One is the individual living being, and the other is the supreme living being. The ordinary living being knows about his body to some extent, but the Supreme, Param\'e4tm\'e4
, knows the condition of all bodies. The individual living being is localized, and the Supreme, Param\'e4tm\'e4, is all-pervading. In this }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7loka}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the word }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 k\'f1etraj\'efa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  refers to an ordinary living being, not the supreme living being. This ordinary living being is of two kinds\emdash }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nitya-baddha}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nitya-mukta.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  One is eternally conditioned and the other eternally liberated. The eternally liberated living beings are in the Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 jagat,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the spiritual world, and they never fall into the material world. Those in the material world are conditioned souls, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nitya-baddha.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nitya-baddhas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 can become liberated by controlling the mind because the cause of conditioned life is the mind. When the mind is trained and the soul is not under the mind's 
control, the soul can be liberated even in this material world. When it is liberated, one is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'e9van-mukta.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  A }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'e9van-mukta}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  knows how he has become conditioned; therefore he tries to purify himself and return home, back to Godhead. The eternally conditi
oned soul is eternally conditioned because he is controlled by the mind. The conditioned state and liberated state are compared to the sleeping, unconscious state and the awakened state. Those who are sleeping and unconscious are eternally conditioned, bu
t those who are awake understand that they are eternally part and parcel of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Therefore even in this material world, they engage in K\'e5\'f1\'eba's service. As confirmed by \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m
\'e9: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e9h\'e4 yasya harer d\'e4sye.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  If one takes to K\'e5\'f1\'eba's service, he is liberated, even though he appears to be a conditioned soul within the material world. }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 J\'e9van-mukta\'f9 sa ucyate.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  In any condition, one is to be considered liberated if his only business is to serve K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.11.13-14
