of different bodies, some moving and some not moving; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 vid\'e4ma}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash we know; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 ni\'f1\'f6h\'e4m}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash annihilation; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 
prabhavam}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash appearance; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 ca}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash and; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 nityam}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash regularly by the principles of nature; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 tat}{
\insrsid11612319 \emdash that; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 n\'e4mata\'f9}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash than simply by name; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 anyat}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash other; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 vyavah\'e4ra-m\'fclam}{
\insrsid11612319 \emdash cause of material activities; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 nir\'fcpyat\'e4m}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash let it be ascertained; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 sat-kriyay\'e4}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash by actual employment; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 anumeyam}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash to be inferred.
\par }\pard\plain \s451\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15405877 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 Al
l of us on the surface of the globe are living entities in different forms. Some of us are moving and some not moving. All of us come into existence, remain for some time and are annihilated when the body is again mingled with the earth. We are all simply
 
different transformations of the earth. Different bodies and capacities are simply transformations of the earth that exist in name only, for everything grows out of the earth and when everything is annihilated it again mingles with the earth. In other wor
ds, we are but dust, and we shall but be dust. Everyone can consider this point.
\par }\pard\plain \s443\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5337272 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Brahma-s\'fctra}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is said: }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 tad-ananyatvam \'e4rabhambha\'eba-\'e7abd\'e4dibhya\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (2.1.14)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
. This cosmic manifestation is a mixture of matter and spirit, but the cause is the Supreme Brahman, the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{
\cf1\insrsid11612319 (1.5.20)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is said: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ida\'e0 hi vi\'e7va\'e0 bhagav\'e4n ivetara\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 The entire cosmic manifestation is but a transformation of the energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but because
 of illusion, no one can appreciate that God is nondifferent from the material world. Actually He is not different, but this material world is simply a transformation of His different energies; }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 par\'e4sya \'e7
aktir vividhaiva \'e7r\'fcyate.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  There are also other versions of this in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sarva\'e0 khalv ida\'e0 brahma.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Matter and spirit are all nondifferent from the Supreme Brahman, Bhagav\'e4n. Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba confirms this statement in the }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{
\cf1\insrsid11612319 7.4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ): }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 me bhinn\'e4 prak\'e5tir a\'f1\'f6adh\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The material energy is K\'e5\'f1\'eba's ener
gy, but it is separated from Him. The spiritual energy is also His energy, but it is not separated from Him. When the material energy is engaged in the service of the Supreme Spirit, so-called material energy is also transformed into spiritual energy, jus
t
 as an iron rod becomes fire when placed in contact with fire. When we can understand by an analytical study that the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the cause of all causes, our knowledge is perfect. Simply understanding the transformations of differen
t energies is partial knowledge. We must come to the ultimate cause. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Na te vidu\'f9 sv\'e4rtha gati\'e0 hi vi\'f1\'ebum.}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid2642478  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
The knowledge of those who are not interested in knowing the original cause of all emanations is never perfect knowledge. There is nothing in the pheno
menal world that is not produced by the supreme energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Aromas from the earth are different scents manufactured and used for different purposes, but the original cause is the earth, nothing else. A waterpot made of ea
r
th can be used to carry water for some time, but ultimately the pot is nothing but earth. Therefore there is no difference between the pot and its original ingredient, earth. It is simply a different transformation of the energy. Originally the cause or p
rimary ingredient is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and the varieties are only by-products. In the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ch\'e4ndogya Upani\'f1ad}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is stated: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yath\'e4
 saumy ekena m\'e5t-pi\'eb\'f2ena sarva\'e0 m\'e5nmaya\'e0 vij\'ef\'e4ta\'e0 sy\'e4d v\'e4c\'e4rambha\'eba\'e0 vik\'e4ro n\'e4madheya\'e0 m\'e5ttikety eva satyam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  If one
 studies the earth, he naturally understands the by-products of the earth. The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  therefore enjoin, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yasmin vij\'ef\'e4te sarvam eva\'e0 vij\'ef\'e4ta
\'e0 bhavati:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  if one simply understands the original cause, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the cause of all causes, then naturally everything else
 is understood, although it may be presented in different varieties. By understanding the original cause of different varieties, one can understand everything. If we understand K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the original cause of everything, we do not need to separately study the subsidiary varieties. Therefore from the very beginning it is said: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 satya\'e0 para\'e0 dh\'e9mahi.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 One has to concentrate one's understanding on the Supreme Truth, K\'e5\'f1\'eba or V\'e4sudeva. The word V\'e4sudeva indicates the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the cause of all causes. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Mat-sth\'e4ni sarva-bh
\'fct\'e4ni na c\'e4ha\'e0 te\'f1v avasthita\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 This is a summary of phenomenal and noumenal philosophy. The phenomenal world depends on the noumenal existence; similarly, everything exists by virtue of the potency of the Supreme Lord, al
though due to our ignorance the Supreme Lord is not perceived in everything.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.12.9
\par }\pard\plain \s275\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13252452 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 TEXT 9
