\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 pra\'e7\'e4ntam}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash the calm and peaceful Supreme Lord, worshiped by the }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 yog\'e9s;}{\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 bhagavat-\'e7abda-sa\'e0j\'efam}{
\insrsid11612319 \emdash known in the higher sense as Bhagav\'e4n, or full of all opulences; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 yat}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash that; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 v\'e4sudevam}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the son of Vasudeva; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 kavaya\'f9}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash the learned scholars; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 vadanti}{\insrsid11612319 \emdash say.
\par }\pard\plain \s451\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15405877 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 
What, then, is the ultimate truth? The answer is that nondual knowledge is the ultimate truth. It is devoid of the contamination of material qualities. It gives us liberation. It is the one without a 
second, all-pervading and beyond imagination. The first realization of that knowledge is Brahman. Then Param\'e4tm\'e4, the Supersoul, is realized by the yog\'e9
s who try to see Him without grievance. This is the second stage of realization. Finally, full realization of the same supreme knowledge is realized in the Supreme Person. All learned scholars describe the Supreme Person as V\'e4
sudeva, the cause of Brahman, Param\'e4tm\'e4 and others.
\par }\pard\plain \s451\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15405877 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is said: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yad advaita\'e0 brahmopani\'f1adi tad apy asya tanu-bh\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 The impersonal Brahman effulgence of the Absolute Truth consists of the bodily rays of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ya \'e4tm\'e4ntary\'e4m\'e9 puru\'f1a iti so 'sy\'e4\'e0\'e7a-vibhava\'f9.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  What is known as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e4tm\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 antary\'e4m\'e9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the Supersoul, is but an expansion o
f the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Sad-ai\'e7varyai\'f9 p\'fcr\'ebo ya iha bhagav\'e4n sa svayam ayam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 What is described as the Supreme Personality of Godhead, complete with all six opulences, is V\'e4sudeva, and \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu is nondifferent from Him. Great learned scholars and philosophers accept this after many, many births. }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 V\'e4sudeva\'f9 sarvam iti sa mah\'e4tm\'e4 sudurlabha\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid548546 (}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid2052598 Bg.}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 7.19}
{\cf1\insrsid548546 )}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 . The wise man can understand that ultimately V\'e4sudeva, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, is the cause of Brahman, and Param\'e4tm\'e4, the Supersoul. Thus V\'e4sudeva is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sarva-k\'e4ra
\'eba-k\'e4ra\'ebam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the cause of all causes. This is confirmed in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The real }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 tattva,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Absolute Truth, is Bhagav\'e4n, but due to incomplete realization of the Absolute Truth, people sometimes describe the same Vi\'f1\'ebu as impersonal Brahman or localized Param\'e4tm\'e4.
\par }\pard\plain \s417\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid8135820 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs416\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid8135820 vadanti tat tattva-vidas\line tattva\'e0 yaj j\'ef
\'e4nam advayam\line brahmeti param\'e4tmeti\line bhagav\'e4n iti \'e7abdyate\line }{\insrsid11612319 (}{\cs347\cf1\insrsid9848435\charrsid9848435 Bh\'e4g.}{\insrsid11612319  }{\i0\insrsid11612319\charrsid2052598 1.2.11)}{\insrsid11612319 
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 From the very beginning, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh
\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  says, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 satya\'e0 para\'e0 dh\'e9mahi:}{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 we meditate on the supreme truth. The supreme truth is explained here as }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'ef\'e4na\'e0 vi\'e7uddha\'e0 satyam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 The Absolute Truth is devoid of material contamination and is transcendental to the material qualities. It gives all spiritual success and liberation from this material world. That Supreme Absolute Truth is K\'e5\'f1\'eba, V\'e4
sudeva. There is no difference between K\'e5\'f1\'eba's inner self and outward body. K\'e5\'f1\'eba is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 p\'fcr\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 the complete whole. There is no distinction between His body and soul as there is between ours. Sometimes so-called scholars, not knowing the constitutional position of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, mislead people by saying that the K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a within is different from the K\'e5\'f1\'eba without. When K\'e5\'f1\'eba says, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 man-man\'e4 bhava mad-bhakto mad-y\'e4j\'e9 m\'e4\'e0 namaskuru,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 so-called scholars advise the reader that it is not the person K\'e5\'f1\'eba to whom we must surrender but the K\'e5\'f1\'eba within. So-called scholars, M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9s, cannot understand K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a with their poor fund of knowledge. One should therefore approach an authorized person to understand K\'e5\'f1\'eba. The spiritual master has actually seen K\'e5\'f1\'eba; therefore he can explain Him properly.
\par }\pard\plain \s417\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid8135820 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs416\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid8135820 tad viddhi pra\'ebip\'e4tena\line paripra\'e7
nena sevay\'e4\line upadek\'f1yanti te j\'ef\'e4na\'e0\line j\'ef\'e4ninas tattva-dar\'e7ina\'f9\line }{\i0\insrsid11612319\charrsid3041504 (Bg. 4.34)
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Without approaching an authorized person, one cannot understand K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.12.12
