by hearing; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 \'e4sv\'e4dana}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash by tasting; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 avaghr\'e4\'eba}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash by smelling; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 sa\'eckalpa}{
\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash by determination; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 vyavas\'e4ya}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash by a conclusion; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 g\'e5ha}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash in the material home; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 gr\'e4mya-upabhogena}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash by material sense gratification; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 kun\'e4thasya}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash of the misguided conditioned soul; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 ajita-\'e4tmana\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash who has not controlled himself; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 yath\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash just as; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 s\'e4rthasya}{
\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash of the living entity interested in sense gratification; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 vilumpanti}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash they plunder.
\par }\pard\plain \s437\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11748500 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 
In the forest of material existence, the uncontrolled senses are like plunderers. The conditioned soul may earn some money for the advancement of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, but unfortunately the uncontrolled s
enses plunder his money through sense gratification. The senses are plunderers because they make one spend his money unnecessarily for seeing, smelling, tasting, touching, hearing, desiring and willing. In this way the conditioned soul is obliged to grati
fy his senses, and thus all his money is spent. This money is actually acquired for the execution of religious principles, but it is taken away by the plundering senses.
\par }\pard\plain \s437\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11748500 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid7153335 P}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'fcrva jamn\'e4rjit\'e4 vidy\'e4 p
\'fcrva janm\'e4rjita\'e0 dhana\'e0 agre dh\'e4vati dh\'e4vati.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  By following the principles of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 one attains a better position in the material world. One may be rich, learned, beautiful or highborn. One who has all these assets should know that they are all meant for the advancement of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. 
Unfortunately, when a person is misguided he misuses his high position for sense gratification. Therefore the uncontrolled senses are considered plunderers. The good position one attains by executing religious principles is wasted as the plundering senses
 take it away. By executing religious principles under the laws of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 var\'eba\'e7rama-dharma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 one is placed in a comfortable position. One may very easily use his assets for the further advancement of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. One should understand that the wealth and o
pportunity one gets in the material world should not be squandered in sense gratification. They are meant for the advancement of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. This K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement is therefore teaching people to control the mind and five knowledge-acqu
iring senses by a definite process. One should practice a little austerity and not spend money on anything other than the regulative life of devotional service. The senses demand that one see beautiful things; therefore money should be spent for decoratin
g
 the Deity in the temple. Similarly, the tongue has to taste good food, which should be bought and offered to the Deity. The nose can be utilized in smelling the flowers offered to the Deity, and the hearing can be utilized by listening to the vibration o
f the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mantra.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  In this way the senses can be regulated and utilized to advance K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness. Thus a good position might not be spoiled by material sense gratification in the form of illicit sex, meat-eating, intoxication and gambling. One s
poils an opulent position in the material world by driving cars, spending time in nightclubs or tasting abominable food in restaurants. In these ways, the plundering senses take away all the assets that the conditioned soul has acquired with great difficu
