\'e5thu\'f1e\'eba begot a son named Nakta in the womb of his wife, named \'c4k\'fcti. Nakta's wife was Druti, and from her womb the great King Gaya was born. Gaya was very famous and pious; he was the best of saintly kings. Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u and His expansions, who are meant to protect the universe, are always situated in the transcendental mode of goodness, known as vi\'e7uddha-sattva. Being the direct expansion of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, King Gaya was also situated in the vi\'e7
uddha-sattva. Because of this, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Gaya was fully equipped with transcendental knowledge. Therefore he was called Mah\'e4puru\'f1a.
