King Gaya gave full protection and security to the citizens so that their personal property would not be disturbed by undesirable elements. He also saw that there was sufficient food to feed all the citizens. }{\fs28\insrsid14632179 [}{
\fs28\insrsid11612319 This is called po\'f1a\'eba.}{\fs28\insrsid14632179 ]}{\fs28\insrsid11612319  He would sometimes distribute gifts to the citizens to satisfy them. }{\fs28\insrsid14632179 [}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 This is called pr\'e9\'ebana.}{
\fs28\insrsid14632179 ]}{\fs28\insrsid11612319  He would sometimes call meetings and satisfy the citizens with sweet words. }{\fs28\insrsid14632179 [}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 This is called upal\'e4lana.}{\fs28\insrsid14632179 ]}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 
 He would also give them good instructions on how to become first-class citizens. }{\fs28\insrsid14632179 [}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 This is called anu\'e7\'e4sana.}{\fs28\insrsid14632179 ]}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 
 Such were the characteristics of King Gaya's royal order. Besides all this, King Gaya
 was a householder who strictly observed the rules and regulations of household life. He performed sacrifices and was an unalloyed pure devotee of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. He was called Mah\'e4puru\'f1
a because as a king he gave the citizens all facil
ities, and as a householder he executed all his duties so that at the end he became a strict devotee of the Supreme Lord. As a devotee, he was always ready to give respect to other devotees and to engage in the devotional service of the Lord. This is the 
b
hakti-yoga process. Due to all these transcendental activities, King Gaya was always free from the bodily conception. He was full in Brahman realization, and consequently he was always jubilant. He did not experience material lamentation. Although he was 
perfect in all respects, he was not proud, nor was he anxious to rule the kingdom.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14632179 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
