\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  when He descends on earth, He has two types of business\emdash to give protection to the faithful and annihilate the demons (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 paritr\'e4\'eb\'e4ya s\'e4dh\'fcn\'e4\'e0 vin\'e4\'e7
\'e4ya ca du\'f1k\'e5t\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). Since the king is the representative of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he is sometimes called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nara-deva,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 that is, the Lord as a human being. According to the Vedic injunctions, he is worshiped as God on the material 
platform. As a representative of the Supreme Lord, the king had the duty to protect the citizens in a perfect way so that they would not be anxious for food and protection and so that they would be jubilant. The king would supply everything for their bene
f
it, and because of this he would levy taxes. If the king or government otherwise levies taxes on the citizens, he becomes responsible for the sinful activities of the citizens. In Kali-yuga, monarchy is abolished because the kings themselves are subjected
 to the influence of Kali-yuga. It is understood from the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 R\'e4m\'e4ya\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  that when Bibh\'e9\'f1a\'eba became friends with Lord R\'e4
macandra, he promised that if by chance or will he broke the laws of friendship with Lord R\'e4macandra, he would become a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or a king in Kali-yuga. In this age, as Bibh\'e9\'f1a
\'eba indicated, both }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and kings are in a wretched condition. Actually there are no kings or }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 in this age, and due to their absence the whole world is in a chaotic condition and is always in distress. Compared to present standards, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Gaya was a true representative of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu; therefore he was known as Mah\'e4puru\'f1a.

\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.15.8
