\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 The seven great sages }{\fs28\insrsid14156474 [}{
\fs28\insrsid11612319 Mar\'e9ci, Vasi\'f1\'f6ha, Atri and so on}{\fs28\insrsid14156474 ]}{\fs28\insrsid11612319  reside on planets beneath Dhruvaloka. Well aware of the influence of the water of the Ganges, to this day they keep Ganges wate
r on the tufts of hair on their heads. They have concluded that this is the ultimate wealth, the perfection of all austerities, and the best means of prosecuting transcendental life. Having obtained uninterrupted devotional service to the Supreme Personal
ity of Godhead, they neglect all other beneficial processes like religion, economic development, sense gratification and even merging into the Supreme. Just as j\'ef\'e4n\'e9
s think that merging into the existence of the Lord is the highest truth, these seven exalted personalities accept devotional service as the perfection of life.
\par }\pard\plain \s440\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12861300 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Transcendentalists are divided into two primary groups: the }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nirvi\'e7e\'f1a-v\'e4d\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or impersonalists, and the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhaktas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 or devotees. The impersonalists do not accept spiritual varieties of life. They want to merge into the existence of the Supreme Lord in His Brahman feature (the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahmajyoti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
). The devotees, however, desire to take part in the transcendental activities of the Supreme Lord. In the upper planetary system, the topmost planet 
is Dhruvaloka, and beneath Dhruvaloka are the seven planets occupied by the great sages, beginning with Mar\'e9ci, Vasi\'f1\'f6
ha and Atri. All these sages regard devotional service as the highest perfection of life. Therefore they all carry the holy water of the G
anges on their heads. This verse proves that for one who has achieved the platform of pure devotional service, nothing else is important, even so-called liberation (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 kaivalya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). \'c7r\'e9la 
\'c7r\'e9dhara Sv\'e4m\'e9 states that only by achieving pure devotional service of the Lord can one give up all other engagements as insignificant. Prabodh\'e4nanda Sarasvat\'e9 confirms his statement as follows:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14156474 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 kaivalya\'e0 narak\'e4yate tri-da\'e7a-p\'fcr \'e4k\'e4\'e7a-pu\'f1p\'e4yate
\line durd\'e4ntendriya-k\'e4la-sarpa-pa\'f6al\'e9 protkh\'e4ta-da\'e0\'f1\'f6r\'e4yate\line vi\'e7va\'e0 p\'fcr\'eba-sukh\'e4yate vidhi-mahendr\'e4di\'e7 ca k\'e9\'f6\'e4yate\line yat k\'e4ru\'ebya-ka\'f6\'e4k\'f1a-vaibhavavat\'e4\'e0 ta\'e0
 gauram eva stuma\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu has perfectly enunciated and broadcast the process of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhakti-yoga.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Consequently, for one who has taken shelter at the lotus feet of \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4pra
bhu, the highest perfection of the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9s, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 kaivalya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or becoming one with the Supreme, is considered hellish, to say nothing of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karm\'e9
s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ' aspiration to be promoted to the heavenly planets. Devotees consider such goals to be worthless phantasmagoria. There are also }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yog\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 who try to control their senses, but they can never succeed without coming to the stage of devotional service. The senses are compared to poisonous snakes, but the senses of a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhakta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 engaged in the service of the Lord are like snakes with their poisonous fangs removed. The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yog\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  tries to suppress his senses, but even great mystics like Vi\'e7v\'e4
mitra fail in the attempt. Vi\'e7v\'e4mitra was conquered by his senses when he was captivated by Menak\'e4 during his meditation. She later gave birth to \'c7akuntal\'e4. The wisest persons in the world, therefore, are the }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhakti-yog\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  as Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba confirms in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 6.47}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
):
