kura informs us that the demigods worship the Supreme Lord in His various Deity forms (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 arc\'e4-vigraha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
) because except in the spiritual world, the Supreme Personality of Godhead cannot be directly worshiped in person. In the material world, the Lord is always worshiped as the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 arc\'e4-vigraha,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 or Deity in the temple. There is no difference between the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 arc\'e4-vigraha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and the original person, and therefore those who are engaged in worshiping the Deity in the temple in full opule
nce, even on this planet, should be understood to be directly in touch with the Supreme Personality of Godhead without a doubt. As enjoined in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7\'e4stras, arcye vi\'f1\'ebau \'e7il\'e4-dh\'e9r guru\'f1u nara-mati
\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "No one should treat the Deity in the temple as stone or metal, nor should one think that the spiritual master is an ordinary human being." One should strictly follow this \'e7\'e4
stric injunction and worship the Deity, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, without offenses. The spiritual master is the direct representat
ive of the Lord, and no one should consider him an ordinary human being. By avoiding offenses against the Deity and the spiritual master, one can advance in spiritual life, or K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In this regard, the following quotation appears in the }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Laghu-bh\'e4gavat\'e4m\'e5ta:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13979563 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 p\'e4dme tu parama-vyomna\'f9\line p\'fcrv\'e4dye dik-catu\'f1\'f6aye\line v
