\par tath\'e4 p\'e4da-vibh\'fctau ca\line nivasanti kram\'e4di me\line jal\'e4v\'e5ti-stha-vaiku\'eb\'f6ha-\line sthita vedavat\'e9-pure
\par satyordhve vai\'f1\'ebave loke\line nity\'e4khye dv\'e4rak\'e4-pure\line \'e7uddhod\'e4d uttare \'e7veta-\line dv\'e9pe cair\'e4vat\'e9-pure
\par k\'f1\'e9r\'e4mbudhi-sthit\'e4nte\line kro\'f2a-parya\'ecka-dh\'e4mani\line s\'e4tvat\'e9ye kvacit tantre\line nava vy\'fch\'e4\'f9 prak\'e9rtit\'e4\'f9\line catv\'e4ro v\'e4sudev\'e4dy\'e4\line n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba-n\'e5si\'e0hakau
\par hayagr\'e9vo mah\'e4-kro\'f2o\line brahm\'e4 ceti navodit\'e4\'f9\line tatra brahm\'e4 tu vij\'efeya\'f9\line p\'fcrvokta-vidhay\'e4 hari\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "In the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Padma Pur\'e4\'eba}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is said that in the spiritual world the Lord personally expands in all directions and is worshiped as V\'e4sudeva, Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eb
a, Pradyumna and Aniruddha. The same God is represented by the Deity in this material world, which is only one quarter of His creation. V\'e4sudeva, Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eb
a, Pradyumna and Aniruddha are also present in the four directions of this material world. There is a Vaiku\'eb\'f6haloka covered with water in this material world, and on that planet is a place called Vedavat\'e9, where V\'e4
sudeva is located. Another planet known as Vi\'f1\'ebuloka is situated above Satyaloka, and there Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eba is present. Similarly, in Dv\'e4rak\'e4-pur\'e9, Pradyumna is the predominator. On the island known as \'c7vetadv\'e9
pa, there is an ocean of milk, and in the midst of that ocean is a place called Air\'e4vat\'e9-pura, where Aniruddha lies on Ananta. In some of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 s\'e4tvata-tantras,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 there is a description of the nine }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 var\'f1as}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and the predominating Deity worshiped in each: (1) V\'e4sudeva, (2) Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eba, (3) Pradyumna, (4) Aniruddha, (5) N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, (6) N\'e5si\'e0ha, (7) Hayagr\'e9va, (8) Mah\'e4var\'e4ha, and (9) Brahm\'e4. "The Lord Brahm\'e4 mentioned in this connection is the Supreme Personality of Godhead. When there is no fit human being to empower as Lord Brahm\'e4
