\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 nirmit\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash created; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 karhi api}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash at any time; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 karma-parva\'eb\'e9m}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash 
which ties the knots of fruitive activity; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 m\'e4y\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash the illusory energy; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 jana\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash a person; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 
ayam}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash this; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 gu\'eba-sarga-mohita\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash bewildered by the three modes of material nature; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 na}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash not; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 veda}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash knows; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 nist\'e4ra\'eba-yogam}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash the process of getting out of material entanglement; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 a\'efjas\'e4
}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash soon; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 tasmai}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash unto Him (the Supreme); }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 nama\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash respectful obeisances; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 te}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash unto You; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 vilaya-udaya-\'e4tmane}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash in whom everything is annihilated and from whom everything is again manifested.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1648073 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 
The illusory energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead binds all of us conditioned souls to this material world. Therefore, without being favored by Him, persons like us cannot understand how to
 get out of that illusory energy. Let me offer my respectful obeisances unto the Lord, who is the cause of creation and annihilation.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1648073 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 K\'e5\'f1\'eba clearly states in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g
\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 7.14}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ):
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6249809 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 daiv\'e9 hy e\'f1\'e4 gu\'eba-may\'e9\line mama m\'e4y\'e4 duratyay\'e4\line 
m\'e4m eva ye prapadyante\line m\'e4y\'e4m et\'e4\'e0 taranti te
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"This divine energy of Mine, consisting of the three modes of material nature, is difficult to overcome. But those who have surrendered unto Me can easily cross beyond it." All conditioned souls working within the illusory energy of the
 Lord consider the body to be the self, and thus they continuously wander throughout the universe, taking birth in different species of life and creating more and more problems. Sometimes they become disgusted with the problems and seek out a process by w
h
ich they can get out of this entanglement. Unfortunately, such so-called research workers are unaware of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and His illusory energy, and thus all of them work only in darkness, never finding a way out. So-called scientists 
a
nd advanced research scholars are ludicrously trying to find the cause of life. They take no notice of the fact that life is already being produced. What will be their credit if they find out the chemical composition of life? All their chemicals are nothi
ng but different transformations of the five elements\emdash earth, water, fire, air and ether. As stated in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 2.20}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
), the living entity is never created (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 na j\'e4yate mriyate v\'e4 kad\'e4cin}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). There are five gross material elements and three minor material el
ements (mind, intelligence and ego), and there are eternal living entities. The living entity desires a certain type of body, and by the order of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, that body is created from material nature, which is nothing but a kind of
 machine handled by the Supreme Lord. The Lord gives the living entity a particular type of mechanical body, and the living entity must work with it according to the law of fruitive activities. Fruitive activities are described in this verse: }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 karma-}{\i\insrsid11805200\charrsid11805200 parva\'eb\'e9\'e0}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  m\'e4y\'e4m.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 The living entity is seated on a machine (the body), and according to the order of the Supreme Lord, he operates the machine. This is the secret of transmigration of the soul from one body to another. The living entity thus becomes entangled in fru
itive activities in this material world. As confirmed in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 15.7}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mana\'f9 \'f1a\'f1
\'f6h\'e4n\'e9ndriy\'e4\'ebi prak\'e5ti-sth\'e4ni kar\'f1ati:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the living entity is struggling very hard against the six senses, which include the mind.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In all the activities of creation and an
nihilation, the living entity is entangled in fruitive activities, which are executed by the illusory energy, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 m\'e4y\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 He is exactly like a computer handled by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The so-called scientists say that nature acts independently, bu
t they cannot explain what nature is. Nature is nothing but a machine operated by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. When one understands the operator, his problems of life are solved. As K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 7.19}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ):
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11805200 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 bah\'fcn\'e4\'e0 janman\'e4m ante\line j\'ef\'e4nav\'e4n m\'e4\'e0
 prapadyate\line v\'e4sudeva\'f9 sarvam iti\line sa mah\'e4tm\'e4 sudurlabha\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"After many births and deaths, he who is actually in knowledge surrenders unto Me, knowing Me to be the cause of all causes and all that is. Such a great soul is very rare." A sane man, therefore, 
surrenders to the Supreme Personality of Godhead and thus gets out of the clutches of the illusory energy, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 m\'e4y\'e4.
\par }\pard\plain \s277\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Thus end the Bhaktivedanta purports of the Fifth Canto, Seventeenth Chapter of the }{\cs341\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  entitled "The Descent of the River Ganges."
\par }\pard\plain \s20\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs20\cf19\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.18: The Prayers Offered to the Lord by the Residents of Jamb\'fcdv\'e9pa
\par }\pard\plain \s73\qc \li0\ri0\sb540\sa540\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0\pararsid5116842 \shading10000\cfpat10 
