\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Foolish materialistic persons do not know how they are being controlled and 
punished at every step by the laws of nature. They think they are very happy in the conditioned state of material life, not knowing the purpose of repeated birth, death, old age and disease. Therefore in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t
\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 7.15}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ) Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba describes such materialistic persons as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 m\'fc\'f2has}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (rascals): }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 na m\'e4\'e0 du\'f1k\'e5tino m\'fc\'f2h\'e4\'f9 prapadyante nar\'e4dham\'e4\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  These }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 m\'fc\'f2has}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 do not know that if they want to purify themselves, they must worship Lord V\'e4sudeva (K\'e5\'f1\'eba) by performing penances and austerities. This purification is the 
aim of human life. This life is not meant for blind indulgence in sense gratification. In the human form, the living being must engage himself in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness to purify his existence: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 tapo divya\'e0
 putrak\'e4 yena sattva\'e0 \'e7uddhyet.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  This is the instruction of King \'c5\'f1abhadeva to His sons. In the human form of life, one must undergo all kinds of austerities to purify his existence. }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Yasm\'e4d brahma-saukhya\'e0 tv anantam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  We are all seeking happiness, but because of our ignorance and foolishness, we cannot know wh
at unobstructed happiness really is. Unobstructed happiness is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahma-saukhya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 spiritual happiness. Although we may get some so-called happiness in this material world, that happiness is temporary. The foolish materialists cannot understand this. Therefore Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja points out, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 m
\'e4y\'e4-sukh\'e4ya bharam udvahato vim\'fc\'f2h\'e4n:}{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 merely for temporary materialistic happiness, these rascals are making huge arrangements, and thus they are baffled life after life.

