\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "One should render transcendental loving service to the Supreme Lord K\'e5
\'f1\'eba favorably and without desire for material profit or gain through fruitive activities or philosophical speculation. That is called pure devotional service." Unless one is complete
ly freed of all material desires, which are caused by the dense darkness of ignorance, one cannot fully engage in the devotional service of the Lord. Therefore we should always offer our prayers to Lord N\'e5si\'e0hadeva, who killed Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu, the personification of material desire. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Hira\'ebya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  means "gold," and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ka\'e7ipu}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 means "a soft cushion or bed." Materialistic persons always desire to make the body comfortable, and for this they require huge amounts of gold. Thus Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was the perfect representative of
 materialistic life. He was therefore the cause of great disturbance to the topmost devotee, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, until Lord N\'e5si\'e0hadeva killed him. Any devotee aspiring to be free of material desires should offer his respectful prayers to N
\'e5si\'e0hadeva as Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja did in this verse.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.18.9
