May there be good fortune throughout the universe, and may all envious persons be pacified. Ma
y all living entities become calm by practicing bhakti-yoga, for by accepting devotional service they will think of each other's welfare. Therefore let us all engage in the service of the supreme transcendence, Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, and always remain absorbed in thought of Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7159422 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 The following verse describes a Vai\'f1\'ebava:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7159422 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 v\'e4\'efch\'e4-kalpa-tarubhya\'e7 ca\line k\'e5p\'e4-sindhubhya eva ca\line 
patit\'e4n\'e4\'e0 p\'e4vanebhyo\line vai\'f1\'ebavebhyo namo nama\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Just like a desire tree, a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava can fulfill all the desires of anyone who takes shelter of his lotus feet. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja is a typical Vai\'f1\'ebava. He prays not for himself, but for all living entities\emdash 
the gentle, the envious and the mischievous. He always thought of the welfare of mischievous persons like his father, Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja did not ask for anything for himself; rather, he prayed for the Lord to excuse his demoniac father. This is the attitude of a Vai\'f1\'ebava, who always thinks of the welfare of the entire universe.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  are meant for persons who are completely free of envy (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 parama-nirmatsar\'e4\'eb\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). Therefore Prahl\'e4
da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja prays in this verse, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 khala\'f9 pras\'e9dat\'e4m:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 "May all the envious persons be pacified." The material world is full of envious persons, but if one frees himself of envy, he becomes liberal in his social dealings and can think of others' welfare. Anyone who takes up K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness and engages himself completely in the service of the Lord cleanses his mind of all envy (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mana\'e7 ca bhadra\'e0 bhajat\'e4d adhok\'f1aje}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). Therefore we should pray to Lord N
\'e5si\'e0hadeva to sit in our hearts. We should pray, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bahir n\'e5si\'e0ho h\'e5daye n\'e5si\'e0ha\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "Let Lord N\'e5si\'e0
hadeva sit in the core of my heart, killing all my bad propensities. Let my mind become clean so that I may peacefully worship the Lord and bring peace to the entire world."
\par \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura has given us a very fine purport in this regard. Whenever one offers a prayer to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, one always requests some benediction from Him. Even pure (}{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ni\'f1k\'e4ma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ) devotees pray for some benediction, as instructed by Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu in His }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7ik\'f1\'e4\'f1\'f6aka:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5194271 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 ayi nanda-tanuja ki\'eckara\'e0\line patita\'e0 m\'e4\'e0 vi\'f1ame bhav\'e4
mbudhau\line k\'e5pay\'e4 tava p\'e4da-pa\'eckaja-\line sthita-dh\'fcl\'e9-sad\'e5\'e7a\'e0 vicintaya}{\i0\cf1\insrsid11612319  
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "O son of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Nanda }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid548546 (}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 K\'e5\'f1\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid548546 )}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 , I am Your e
ternal servitor, yet somehow or other I have fallen into the ocean of birth and death. Please pick Me up from the ocean of death and place Me as one of the atoms at Your lotus feet." In another prayer Lord Caitanya says, }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mama janmani janman\'e9\'e7vare bhavat\'e4d bhaktir ahaituk\'e9 tvayi:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "Life after life, kindly let Me have unalloyed love and devotion at Your Lordship's lotus feet." When Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja chants }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 o\'e0 namo bhagavate narasi\'e0h\'e4ya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  he prays for a benediction from the Lord, but because he is also an exalted Vai\'f1\'eb
ava, he wants nothing for his personal sense gratification. The first desire expressed in his prayer is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 svasty astu vi\'e7vasya:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 "Let there be good fortune throughout the entire universe." Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja thus requested the Lord to be merciful to everyone, including his father, a most envious person. According to C\'e4\'ebakya Pa\'eb\'f2
ita, there are two kinds of envious living entities: one is a snake, and the other is the man like Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu, who is by nature envious of everyone, even of his father or son. Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was envious of his little son Prahl\'e4
da, but Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja asked a benediction for the benefit of his father. Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was very envious of devotees, but Prahl\'e4da wished that his father and other demons like him would give up their env
ious nature by the grace of the Lord and stop harassing the devotees (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 khala\'f9 pras\'e9dat\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). The difficulty is that the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 khala}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (envious living entity) is rarely pacified. One kind of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 khala,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the snake, can be pacified simply by }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mantras}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or by the action of a particular herb (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mantrau\'f1adhi-va\'e7a\'f9 sarpa\'f9 khalakena niv\'e4ryate}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
). An envious person, however, cannot be pacified by any means. Therefore Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja prays that all envious persons may undergo a change of heart and think of the welfare of others.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 If the K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement spreads all over the world, and if by the grace of K\'e5\'f1\'eba everyone accepts it, the thinking of envious people will change. Everyone will think of the welfare of others. Therefore Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja prays, }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7iva\'e0 mitho dhiy\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  In material activities, everyone is envious of others, but in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, no one is envious of anyone else; everyone thinks of the welfare of others. Therefore Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja prays that everyone's mind may become gentle by being fixed at the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhajat\'e4d adhok\'f1aje}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). As indicated elsewhere in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sa vai mana
\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pad\'e4ravindayo\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ) and as advised by Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 18.65}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), 
}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 man-man\'e4 bhava mad-bhakta\'f9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  one should constantly think of the lotus feet of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Then one's mind will certainly be cleansed (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
ceto-darpa\'eba-m\'e4rjanam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). Materialists always think of sense gratification, but Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja prays that the Lord's mercy will change their minds and they will stop thinking of sense gratification. If they th
ink of K\'e5\'f1\'eba always, everything will be all right. Some people argue that if everyone thought of K\'e5\'f1\'eba in that way, the whole universe would be vacated because everyone would go back home, back to Godhead. However, \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van
\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura says that this is impossible because the living entities are innumerable. If one set of living entities is actually delivered by the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement, another set will fill the entire universe.

\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.18.10
\par }\pard\plain \s275\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13252452 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 TEXT 10
