a is the original source of all living entities. This is confirmed in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 15.7}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), wherein K\'e5\'f1\'eba says:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1319750 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 mamaiv\'e4\'e0\'e7o j\'e9va-loke\line j\'e9va-bh\'fcta\'f9 san\'e4tana\'f9
\line mana\'f9 \'f1a\'f1\'f6h\'e4n\'e9ndriy\'e4\'ebi\line prak\'e5ti-sth\'e4ni kar\'f1ati
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"The living entities in this conditioned world are My eternal, fragmental parts. Due to conditioned life, they are struggling very hard with the six senses, which include the mind." All living entities are part and parcel of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, and therefore when they revive their original K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, they possess all the good qualities of K\'e5\'f1\'eba in a small quantity. When one engages himself in the nine processes of devotional service (}{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7rava\'eba\'e0 k\'e9rtana\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9 smara\'eba\'e0 p\'e4da-sevanam/ arcana\'e0 vandana}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid8586718 \'e0 d\'e4sya\'e0 sakhyam \'e4tma-nivedanam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
), one's heart becomes purified, and he immediately understands his relationship with K\'e5\'f1\'eba. He then revives his original quality of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c4di-l\'e9l\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Chapter Eight, there is a description of some of the qualities of devotees. For example, \'c7r\'e9 Pa\'eb\'f2ita Harid\'e4
sa is described as being very well-behave
d, tolerant, peaceful, magnanimous and grave. In addition, he spoke very sweetly, his endeavors were very pleasing, he was always patient, he respected everyone, he always worked for everyone's benefit, his mind was free of duplicity, and he was completel
y devoid of all malicious activities. These are all originally qualities of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and when one becomes a devotee they automatically become manifest. \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'ebad\'e4sa Kavir\'e4ja, the author of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  says that all good qualities become manifest in the body of a Vai\'f1\'ebava and that only by the presence of these good qualities can one distinguish a Vai\'f1\'ebava from a non-Vai\'f1\'ebava. K\'e5
\'f1\'ebad\'e4sa Kavir\'e4ja lists the following twenty-six good qualities of a Vai\'f1\'ebava: }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (1)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is very kind to everyone. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (2)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 He does not make anyone his enemy. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (3)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is truthful. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (4)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is equal to everyone. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (5)}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  No one can find any fault in him. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (6)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is magnanimous. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (7)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is mild. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (8)}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is always clean. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (9)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is without possessions. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (10)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He works for everyone's benefit. }{
\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (11)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is very peaceful. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (12)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is always surrendered to K\'e5\'f1\'eba. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (13)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 He has no material desires. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (14)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is very meek. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (15)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is steady. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (16)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 He controls his senses. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (17)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He does not eat more than required. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (18)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is not influenced by the Lord's illusory energy. }{
\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (19)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He offers respect to everyone. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (20)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He does not desire any respect for himself. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (21)}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is very grave. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (22)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is merciful. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (23)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is friendly. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (24)}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is poetic. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (25)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is expert. }{\b\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 (26)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is silent.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.18.13
