\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  dehi.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "O worshipable mother Durg\'e4dev\'e9, please give me wealth, strength, fame, a good wife and so on." By pleasing goddess Durg\'e4 one can obtain such benef
its, but since they are temporary, they result only in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 m\'e4y\'e4-sukha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (illusory happiness). As stated by Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 m\'e4y\'e4-sukh\'e4
ya bharam udvahato vim\'fc\'f2h\'e4n:}{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 those who work very hard for material benefits are }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vim\'fc\'f2has,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
