\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is said that no one can receive the real favor of the Supreme Personality of Godhead without following in the footsteps of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 gop\'e9s.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 Even the goddess of fortune could not receive the same favor as the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 gop\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  although she underwent severe austerities and penances for many years. Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu discusses this point with Vye\'ecka\'f6a Bha\'f6\'f6a in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11612319 Madhya}{\cf1\insrsid11612319  9.111-131)}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 : "The Lord inquired from Vye\'ecka\'f6a Bha\'f6\'f6a, 'Your worshipable goddess of fortune, Lak\'f1m\'e9, always remains on the chest of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, and she is certainly the most 
chaste woman in the creation. However, My Lord is Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba, a cowherd boy engaged in tending cows. Why is it that Lak\'f1m\'e9, being such a chaste wife, wants to associate with My Lord? Just to associate with K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Lak\'f1m
\'e9 abandoned all transcendental happiness in Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha and for a long time accepted vows and regulative principles and performed unlimited austerities.'
\par "Vye\'ecka\'f6a Bha\'f6\'f6a replied, 'Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba are one and the same, but the pastimes of K\'e5\'f1\'eba are more relishable due to their sportive nature. They are very pleasing for K\'e5\'f1\'eba's }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7aktis.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Since K\'e5\'f1\'eba and N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba are both the same personality, Lak\'f1m\'e9's association with K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a did not break her vow of chastity. Rather, it was in great fun that the goddess of fortune wanted to associate with Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. The goddess of fortune considered that her vow of chastity would not be damaged by her relationship with K\'e5\'f1
\'eba. Rather, by associating with K\'e5\'f1\'eba she could enjoy the benefit of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 r\'e4sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  dance. If she wanted to enjoy herself with K\'e5\'f1\'eba wh
at fault is there? Why are you joking so about this?'
\par "Lord Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu replied, 'I know that there is no fault in the goddess of fortune, but still she could not enter into the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 r\'e4sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 dance. We hear this from revealed scriptures. The authorities of Vedic knowledge met Lord R\'e4macandra in Da\'eb\'f2ak\'e4ra\'ebya, and by their penances and austerities, they were allowed to enter into the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 r\'e4sa}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  dance. But can you tell me why the goddess of fortune, Lak\'f1m\'e9, could not get that opportunity? '
\par "To this Vye\'ecka\'f6a Bha\'f6\'f6a r
eplied, 'I cannot enter into the mystery of this incident. I am an ordinary living being. My intelligence is limited, and I am always disturbed. How can I understand the pastimes of the Supreme Lord? They are deeper than millions of oceans.'
\par "Lord Caitanya replied, 'Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba has a specific characteristic. He attracts everyone's heart by the mellow of His personal conjugal love. By following in the footsteps of the inhabitants of the planet known as Vrajaloka or Goloka V\'e5nd\'e4
vana, one can attain the shelter of the lotus feet of \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba. However, the inhabitants of that planet do not know that Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Unaware that K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is the Supreme Lord, the residents of V\'e5nd\'e4vana like Nanda Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Ya\'e7od\'e4dev\'e9 and the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 gop\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  treat K\'e5\'f1\'eba as their beloved son or lover. Mother Ya\'e7od\'e4
 accepts Him as her son and sometimes binds Him to a grinding mortar. K\'e5\'f1\'eba's cowherd boy friends think He is an ordinary boy and get up on His shoulders. In Goloka V\'e5nd\'e4vana no one has any desire other than to love K\'e5\'f1\'eba.' "

\par The conclusion is that one cannot associate with K\'e5\'f1\'eba unless he has fully received the favor of the inhabitants of Vrajabh\'fcmi. Therefore if one wants to be delivered by K\'e5\'f1\'eba directly, he must take to the service of the residents of
 V\'e5nd\'e4vana, who are unalloyed devotees of the Lord.
