ght are the formless energies of fire, and in that sense they are unreal. Only the fire has form, and therefore it is the real form of the heat and light. As K\'e5\'f1\'eba states in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 9.4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 may\'e4 tatam ida\'e0 sarva\'e0 jagad avyakta-m\'fcrtin\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "By Me, in My unmanifested form}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4025764 , t}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 his entire universe is pervaded." Thus the impersonal conception of the Lord is like the expansion of heat and light from a fire. In }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the Lord also says, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mat-sth\'e4ni sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni na c\'e4ha\'e0 te\'f1v avasthita\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the entire material creation is resting on K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a's energy, either material, spiritual or marginal, but because His form is absent from the expansion of His energy, He is not personally present. This inconceivable expansion of the Supreme Lord's energy is called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
acintya-\'e7akti.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Therefore no one can understand the real form of the Lord without becoming His devotee.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.18.32
