\'e4ram akarod bhuvane\'f1u kintu\line k\'e5\'f1\'eba\'f9 svaya\'e0 samabhavat parama\'f9 pum\'e4n yo\line govindam \'e4di-puru\'f1a\'e0 tam aha\'e0 bhaj\'e4mi
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"I worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Govinda, who is always situated in various incarnations such as R\'e4ma, N\'e5si\'e0ha and many subincarnations as well, but who is the original Personality of Godhead known as K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a and who incarnates personally also." K\'e5\'f1\'eba, who is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vi\'f1\'ebu-tattva,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  has expanded Himself in many Vi\'f1\'ebu forms, of which Lord R\'e4macandra is one. We know that the }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vi\'f1\'ebu-tattva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is carried by the transcendental bird Garu\'f2a and is equipped with different types of weapons in four hands. Therefore we may doubt whether Lord R\'e4
macandra could be in the same category, since He was carried by Hanum\'e4n, not by Garu\'f2a, and had neither four hands nor the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7a\'eckha, cakra, gad\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 padma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Consequently this verse clarifies that R\'e4macandra is as good as K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 r\'e4m\'e4di-m\'fcrti\'f1u kal\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
). Although K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the original Supreme Personality of Godhead, R\'e4macandra is not different from Him. R\'e4macandra is unaffected by the modes of material nature, and therefore He is }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 pra\'e7\'e4nta,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  never disturbed by those modes.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Unless one is saturated with love for the Supreme Personality of Godhead, one cannot appreciate the transcendental value of Lord R\'e4macandra; one cannot see Him with material eyes. Because demons like R\'e4va\'eb
a have no spiritual vision, they consider Lord R\'e4macandra an ordinary }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 k\'f1atriya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  king. R\'e4va\'eba therefore attempted to kidnap Lord R\'e4macandra's eternal consort, S\'e9t\'e4dev\'e9
. Actually, however, R\'e4va\'eba could not carry off S\'e9t\'e4dev\'e9 in her original form. As soon as she was touched by R\'e4va\'eb
a's hands, she gave him a material form, but she maintained her original form beyond his vision. Therefore in this verse the words }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 pratyak pra\'e7\'e4ntam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  indicate that Lord R\'e4
macandra and His potency, the goddess S\'e9t\'e4, keep themselves aloof from the influence of the material energy.
\par In the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Upani\'f1ads}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is said: }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yam eva}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4981060 i\'f1a v\'e5\'ebute tena labhya\'f9}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 .}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The Supreme Lord, Param\'e4tm\'e4, the Personality of Godhead, can be seen or perceived only by persons who are saturated with devotional service. As stated in the }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (5.38)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4981060 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 prem\'e4\'efjana-cchurita-bhakti-vilocanena\line santa\'f9 sadaiva h\'e5daye
\'f1u vilokayanti\line ya\'e0 \'e7y\'e4masundaram acintya-gu\'eba-svar\'fcpa\'e0\line govindam \'e4di-puru\'f1a\'e0 tam aha\'e0 bhaj\'e4mi
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "I worship the primeva
l Lord, Govinda, who is always seen by the devotee whose eyes are anointed with the pulp of love. He is seen in His eternal form of \'c7y\'e4masundara, situated within the heart of the devotee." Similarly, in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ch\'e4
ndogya Upani\'f1ad}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is stated, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 et\'e4s tisro devat\'e4 anena j\'e9vena.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  In this verse of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ch\'e4ndogya Upani\'f1ad}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 anena}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is used to distinguish the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e4tm\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and Param\'e4tm\'e4
 as two separate identities. The words }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 tisro devat\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  indicate that the body of the living entity is made of three material elements\emdash fire, earth and water. Although the Param\'e4tm
\'e4 enters the heart of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'e9v\'e4tm\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  who is influenced and designated by a material body, the Param\'e4tm\'e4 has nothing to do with the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'e9v
\'e4tm\'e4's}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  body. Because the Param\'e4tm\'e4 has no material connections, He is described here as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 an\'e4ma-r\'fcpa\'e0 niraham.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The Param\'e4tm\'e4
 has no material identity, whereas the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'e9v\'e4tm\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  does. The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'e9v\'e4tm\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 may introduce himself as an Indian, American, German and so on, but the Param\'e4tm\'e4 has no such material designations, and therefore He has no material name. The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'e9v\'e4tm\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 is different from his name, but the Param\'e4tm\'e4 is not; His name and He Himself are one and the same. This is the meaning of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 niraham,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 which means "without material designations." This word cannot possibly be twisted to mean that the Param\'e4tm\'e4 has no }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 aha\'eck\'e4ra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 no "I-ness" or identity. He has His transcendental identity as the Supreme. This is the explanation given by \'c7r\'e9la J\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9. According to another interpretation, given by Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura, }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 niraham}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  means }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nirni\'e7cayena aham.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Niraham}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 does not mean that the Supreme Lord has no identity. Rather, the stress given by the word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 aham}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  proves strongly that He does have His personal identity because }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nir}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  not only means "negative" but also means "strong ascertainment."
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.19.5
