\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4981060 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 It was ordained that R\'e4va\'eba, chief of the R\'e4k\'f1
asas, could not be killed by anyone but a man, and for this reason Lord R\'e4macandra, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, appeared in the form of a human being. Lord R\'e4macandra's mission, however, was not only to kill R\'e4va\'eb
a but also to teach mortal beings that material happiness centered around sex life or centered around one's w
ife is the cause of many miseries. He is the self-sufficient Supreme Personality of Godhead, and nothing is lamentable for Him. Therefore why else could He be subjected to tribulations by the kidnapping of mother S\'e9t\'e4?
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4981060 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 When the Lord appears in this
 universe in the form of a human being, He has two purposes, as stated in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid548546 (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11612319 4.8}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid548546 )}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 paritr\'e4\'eb\'e4ya s\'e4dh\'fcn\'e4\'e0 vin\'e4\'e7\'e4ya ca du\'f1k\'e5t\'e4m:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 to destroy the demons and protect the devotees. To protect the devotees, the Lord not only satisfies them by His personal presence but also teaches them so that they will not fall down from devotional service. By His personal example, Lord R\'e4
macandra taught the devotees that it is better not to enter married life, which is certainly followed by many tribulations. As confirmed in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{
\cs337\cf1\insrsid548546 (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 7.9.45}{\cf1\insrsid548546 )}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10510610 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 yan maithun\'e4di-g\'e5hamedhi-sukha\'e0 hi tuccha\'e0\line ka\'eb\'f2\'fc
yanena karayor iva du\'f9kha-du\'f9kham\line t\'e5pyanti neha k\'e5pa\'eb\'e4 bahu-du\'f9kha-bh\'e4ja\'f9\line ka\'eb\'f2\'fctivan manasija\'e0 vi\'f1aheta-dh\'e9ra\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 K\'e5pa\'ebas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 those who are not advanced in spiritual knowledge and who are therefore just the opposite of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 generally take to family life, which is a concession for sex. Thus they enjoy sex again and again, although that sex is followed by many tribulations. This is a warning to devotees. To teach this lesson to devotees and to human society in general, Lord 
\'c7r\'e9 R\'e4macandra, although the Supreme Personality of Godhead Himself, underwent a series of tribulations because He accepted a wife, mother S\'e9t\'e4. Lord R\'e4macandra underwent these austerities, of course, only to
 instruct us; actually He never has any reason to lament for anything.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Another aspect of the Lord's instructions is that one who accepts a wife must be a faithful husband and give her full protection. Human society is divided into two classes of men\emdash those 
who strictly follow the religious principles and those who are devotees. By His personal example, Lord R\'e4
macandra wanted to instruct both of them how to fully adopt the discipline of the religious system and how to be a beloved and dutiful husband. Otherwi
se He had no reason to undergo apparent tribulations. One who strictly follows religious principles must not neglect to provide all facilities for the complete protection of his wife. There may be some suffering because of this, but one must nevertheless 
endure it. That is the duty of a faithful husband. By His personal example, Lord R\'e4macandra demonstrated this duty. Lord R\'e4macandra could have produced hundreds and thousands of S\'e9t\'e4
s from His pleasure energy, but just to show the duty of a faithful husband, He not only rescued S\'e9t\'e4 from the hands of R\'e4va\'eba but also killed R\'e4va\'eba and all the members of his family.
\par Another aspect of the teachings of Lord R\'e4macandra is that although Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and His devotees may apparently suffer from material tribulations, they have nothing to do with such tribulations. They are }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mukta-puru\'f1as,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  liberated persons, under all circumstances. It is therefore said in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Caitanya-bh\'e4gavata:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10510610 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 yata dekha vai\'f1\'ebavera vyavah\'e4ra du\'f9kha\line ni\'e7caya j\'e4
niha t\'e4h\'e4 param\'e4nanda-sukha
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 A Vai\'f1\'eb
ava is always firmly situated in transcendental bliss because of engagement in devotional service. Although he may appear to suffer material pains, his position is called transcendental bliss in separation (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 viraha}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). The emotions a lover and beloved feel when separated from one another are actually very blissful, although apparently painful. Therefore the separation of Lord R\'e4macandra from S\'e9t\'e4dev\'e9
, as well as the consequent tribulation they suffered, is but another display of transcendental bliss. That is the opinion of \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.19.6
