\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the body of eternity, transcendental bliss and full knowledge. Now in this verse He is more fully described. K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is the creator of the entire cosmic manifestation, yet He is unattached to it. If we were to construct a very tall skyscraper, we would be very attached to it, but K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is so renounced that although He has created everything, He is not attached to anything (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 na badhyate}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). Furthermore, although K\'e5\'f1\'eba has His transcendental form, }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is not disturbed by the bodily necessities of life, which are called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 daihika;}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 for example, He is never hungry, thirsty or fatigued (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 na hanyate deha-gato 'pi daihikai\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). Then again, since everything is K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a's property, He sees everything and is present everywhere, but because His body is transcendental, He is
 above vision, the objects of vision and the process of vision. When we see someone beautiful, we are attracted. The sight of a beautiful woman immediately attracts a man, and the sight of a man naturally attracts a woman. K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, however, is transcendental to all these faults. Although He is the seer of everything, He is not afflicted with faulty vision (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 na d\'e5g yasya gu\'ebair vid\'fc\'f1yate}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
). Therefore, although He is the witness and seer, He is aloof from all affection for the activities He sees. He is always unattached and separate; He is only a witness.
