\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Mah\'e4tm\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  advanced devotees, worship only the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Others, however, who are also sometimes called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mah\'e4tm\'e4s,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  worship the Lord as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid12215454 ekatvena p\'e5thaktvena}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 .}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  In other words, they accept the demigods as different parts of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a and worship them for various benedictions. Although the devotees of the demigods thus achieve the desired results offered by K\'e5\'f1\'eba, they have been described in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid12215454 h\'e5ta-j\'ef\'e4nah}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  not very intelligent. K\'e5\'f1\'eba does not desire to be worshiped indirectly through the different parts of His body; K\'e5
\'f1\'eba wants direct devotional worship. Therefore a devotee who directly worships Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba through staunch devotional service, as recommended in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 t\'e9vre\'eba bhakti-yogena yajeta puru\'f1a\'e0 param}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
), is very quickly elevated to the transcendental position. Nevertheless, devotees who worship the demigods, the different parts of the Lord, receive the benedictions they desire because the Lord 
is the original master of all benedictions. If anyone wants a particular benediction, for the Lord to award it is not at all difficult.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.19.27
