\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 di\'e7ati}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash He offers; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 arthitam}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash the object prayed for; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 arthita\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash 
being prayed to; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 n\'e5\'eb\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash by the human beings; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 na}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash not; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 eva}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash 
indeed; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 artha-da\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash the bestower of benedictions; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 yat}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash which; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 puna\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 
\emdash again; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 arthit\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash a demand for a benediction; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 yata\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash from which; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 svayam}{
\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash personally; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 vidhatte}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash He gives; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 bhajat\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash unto those engaged in His service; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 anicchat\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash although not desiring it; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 icch\'e4-pidh\'e4nam}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash which covers all desirable things; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 
nija-p\'e4da-pallavam}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash His own lotus feet.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2503249 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 
The Supreme Personality of Godhead fulfills the material desires of a devotee who
 approaches Him with such motives, but He does not bestow benedictions upon the devotee that will cause him to demand more benedictions again. However, the Lord willingly gives the devotee shelter at His own lotus feet, even though such a person does not 
aspire for it, and that shelter satisfies all his desires. That is the Supreme Personality's special mercy.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2503249 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
The devotees mentioned in the previous verse approach the Supreme Personality of Godhead with material motives, but this verse explains how such devotees are saved from those desires. }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid548546 (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 2.3.10}{\cf1\insrsid548546 )}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  advises:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2503249 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 ak\'e4ma\'f9 sarva-k\'e4mo v\'e4\line mok\'f1a-k\'e4ma ud\'e4ra-dh\'e9\'f9
\line t\'e9vre\'eba bhakti-yogena\line yajeta puru\'f1a\'e0 param
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"Whether one is freed from all material desires, is full of material desires, or desires to
 become one with the Supreme, he should engage in devotional service." In this way, not only will the devotee's desires be fulfilled, but the day will come when he will have no other desire than to serve the lotus feet of the Lord. One who engages in the 
service of the Lord with some motive is called a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sak\'e4ma-bhakta,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and one who serves the Lord without any motives is called an }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ak\'e4ma-bhakta.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  K\'e5\'f1\'eba is so merciful that He turns a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sak\'e4ma-bhakta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  into an }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ak\'e4ma-bhakta.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 A pure devotee, an }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ak\'e4ma-bhakta,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  who has no material motives, is satisfied simply to serve the lotus feet of the Lord. This is confirmed in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g
\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 6.22}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ya\'e0 labdhv\'e4 c\'e4para\'e0 l\'e4bha\'e0 manyate n\'e4dhika\'e0 tata\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 if one engages in the service of the lotus feet of the Lord, he does not want anything more. This is the highest stage of devotional service. The Lord is so kind even to a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sak\'e4ma-bhakta,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 a motivated devotee, that He satisfies his desires in such a way that one day he becomes an }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ak\'e4ma-bhakta.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, for example, became a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
bhakta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  with the motive of getting a better kingdom than that of his father, but finally he became an }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ak\'e4ma-bhakta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and said to the Lord, }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sv\'e4min k\'e5t\'e4rtho'smi vara\'e0 na y\'e4ce:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "My dear Lord, I am very satisfied simply to serve Your lotus feet. I do not want any material be
nefits." Sometimes it is found that a small child eats dirty things, but his parents take away the dirty things and offer him a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sande\'e7a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 or some other sweetmeat. Devotees who aspire for material benedictions are compared to such children. The Lord is so kin
d that He takes away their material desires and gives them the highest benediction. Therefore, even for material motives, one should not worship anyone other than the Supreme Personality of Godhead; one must fully engage himself in the devotional service 
of the Lord so that all his desires will be fulfilled and at the end he can go back home, back to Godhead. This is explained in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Madhya}{\cf1\insrsid11612319  22.37-39, 41}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ) as follows.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Anyak\'e4m\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash 
a devotee may desire something other than service to the lotus feet of the Lord; }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 yadi kare k\'e5\'f1\'ebera bhajana}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash but if he engages in Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba's service; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 n\'e4 m\'e4giteha k\'e5\'f1\'eba t\'e4re dena sva-cara\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash K\'e5\'f1\'eba gives him shelter at His lotus feet, even though he does not aspire for it. }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 K\'e5\'f1\'eba kahe}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash the Lord says; }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e4m\'e4 bhaje}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash "He is engaged in My service"; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 m\'e4ge vi\'f1aya-sukha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash "but he wants the benefits of material sense gratification." }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Am\'e5ta ch\'e4\'f2i' vi\'f1a m\'e4ge:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash "such a devotee is like a person who asks for poison instead of nectar." }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ei ba\'f2a m\'fcrkha:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "That is his foolishness." }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ami-vij\'efa:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "But I am experienced." }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ei m\'fcrkhe 'vi\'f1aya' kene diba:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 "Why should I give such a foolish person the dirty things of material enjoyment?" }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Sva-cara\'eba-m\'e5ta:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "It would be better for Me to give him shelter at My lotus feet." }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 'Vi\'f1aya' bhul\'e4iba:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "I shall cause him to forget all material desires." }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 K\'e4ma l\'e4gi' k\'e5\'f1\'eba bhaje}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash 
if one engages in the service of the Lord for sense gratification; }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 paya k\'e5\'f1\'eba-rase}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \emdash the result is that he ultimately gets a taste for serving the lotus feet of the Lord. }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 K\'e4ma ch\'e4\'f2i' 'd}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10292926 \'e4s}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 a' haite haya abhil\'e4\'f1e:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  
He then gives up all material desires and wants to become an eternal servant of the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.19.28
