\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1447867 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 
We are now living in the heavenly planets, undoubtedly as a result of our having performed ritualistic ceremonies, pious activities and yaj\'efas and having studied the Vedas. However, our lives here will one day be finished. We pray t
hat at that time, if any merit remains from our pious activities, we may again take birth in Bh\'e4rata-var\'f1a as human beings able to remember the lotus feet of the Lord. The Lord is so kind that He personally comes to the land of Bh\'e4rata-var\'f1
a and expands the good fortune of its people.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1447867 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
It is certainly as a result of pious activities that one takes birth in the heavenly planets, but from those planets one must nevertheless come down again to earth, as stated in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 k\'f1\'e9\'ebe pu\'ebye martya-loka\'e0 vi\'e7anti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
). Even the demigods must return to earth to work like ordinary men when the results of their pious activities expire. Nevertheless, the demigods desire to come to the land of Bh\'e4rata-var\'f1a if even a small portion of the merits of their pious activi
ties remains. In other words, to take birth in Bh\'e4rata-var\'f1a, one must perform more pious activities than the demigods. In Bh\'e4rata-var\'f1a one is naturally K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious, and if one further cultivates his K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, by the grace of K\'e5\'f1\'eba he certainly expands his good fortune by becoming perfect in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness and very easily going back home, back to Godhead. In many other places in the Vedic literature it is found that even the demigods want to come to this land of Bh\'e4rata-var\'f1a. A foolish
 person may desire to be promoted to the heavenly planets as a result of his pious activities, but even the demigods from the heavenly planets want to come to Bh\'e4rata-var\'f1a and achieve bodies that may be very easily used to cultivate K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness. Therefore \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu repeatedly says:
