tion of various islands, beginning with Plak\'f1adv\'e9pa, and the oceans that surround them. There is also a description of the location and dimensions of the mountain known as Lok\'e4loka. The island of Plak\'f1adv\'e9pa, which is twice as broad as Jamb
\'fcdv\'e9pa, is surrounded by an ocean of salt water. The master of this island is Idhmajihva, one of the sons of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Priyavrata. The island is divided into seven regions, each with a mountain and a large river.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6756111 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid13582514\charrsid6756111 The second island is called S\'e4lmal\'e9dv\'e9
