pa, this island is also divided into seven regions, each with a mountain and a very large river. The inhabitants of this island worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the form of Candr\'e4tm\'e4.
\par The third island, which is surrounded by an ocean of clarified butter and is also divided into seven regions, is called Ku\'e7adv\'e9pa. Its master is Hira\'ebyaret\'e4, another son of Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Priyavrata, and its inhabitants worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the form of Agni, the fire-god. The width of this island is 6,400,000 miles, or, in other words, twice the width of S\'e4lmal\'e9dv\'e9pa.
\par The fourth island, Krau\'efcadv\'e9pa, which is surrounded by an ocean of milk, is 12,800,000 miles wide and is also divided, like the others, into seven regions, each with a large mountain and a large river. The master of this island is Gh\'e5tap\'e5\'f1
\'f6ha, another son of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Priyavrata. The inhabitants of this island worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the form of water.
\par The fifth island, \'c7\'e4kadv\'e9pa, which is 25,600,000 miles wide, is surrounded by an ocean of yogurt. Its master is Medh\'e4tithi, another son of Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Priyavrata. It is also divided into seven regions, each with a large mountain and a large river. Its inhabitants worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the form of V\'e4yu, air.
\par The sixth island, Pu\'f1karadv\'e9pa, which is twice as wide as the previous island, is surrounded by an ocean of clear water. Its master is V\'e9tihotra, another son of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Priyavrata. The island is divided in two by a large mountain named M
\'e4nasottara. The inhabitants of this island worship Svayambh\'fc, another feature of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Beyond Pu\'f1karadv\'e9
pa there are two islands, one always lit by the sunshine and the other always dark. Between them is a mountain called Lok\'e4loka, which is situated one billion miles from the edge of the universe. Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba
, expanding His opulence, resides upon this mountain. The area beyond Lok\'e4loka Mountain is called Aloka-var\'f1a, and beyond Aloka-var\'f1a is the pure destination of persons who desire liberation.
\par Vertically, the sun-globe is situated just in the middle of the universe, in Antarik\'f1a, the space between Bh\'fcrloka and Bhuvarloka. The distance between the sun and the circumference of A\'eb\'f2
a-golaka, the globe of the universe, is estimated to be twenty-five }{\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid13582514\charrsid15470471 ko\'f6i yojanas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid13582514\charrsid6756111  (two billion miles). Because the sun enters the uni
