\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 tray\'e9-mayam}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash established in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 Vedas;}{\fs28\insrsid11612319  }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 s\'fcryam \'e4tm\'e4nam}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash 
the Supersoul, represented by the sun-god; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 yajante}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash they worship.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16462443 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 The seven islands }{\fs28\insrsid6234997 [}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 
var\'f1as}{\fs28\insrsid16462443 ]}{\fs28\insrsid11612319  are named according to the names of those seven sons\emdash \'c7iva, Yavasa, Subhadra, \'c7\'e4nta, K\'f1ema, Am\'e5ta and Abhaya. In those seven
 tracts of land, there are seven mountains and seven rivers. The mountains are named Ma\'ebik\'fc\'f6a, Vajrak\'fc\'f6a, Indrasena, Jyoti\'f1m\'e4n, Supar\'eba, Hira\'ebya\'f1\'f6h\'e9va and Megham\'e4la, and the rivers are named Aru\'eb\'e4, N\'e5m\'eb
\'e4, \'c4\'ecgiras\'e9, S\'e4vitr\'e9, Suptabh\'e4t\'e4, \'c5tambhar\'e4 and Satyambhar\'e4. One can immediately be free from material contamination by touching or bathing in those rivers, and the four castes of people who live in Plak\'f1adv\'e9pa
\emdash the Ha\'e0sas, Pata\'ecgas, \'dcrdhv\'e4yanas and Saty\'e4\'ecgas\emdash purify themselves in that way. The inhabitants of Plak\'f1adv\'e9
pa live for one thousand years. They are beautiful like the demigods, and they also beget children like the demigods. By completely performing the ritualistic ceremonies mentioned in the Vedas and by worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead as
 represented by the sun-god, they attain the sun, which is a heavenly planet.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16462443 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 According to general understanding, there are originally three deities\emdash 
Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and Lord \'c7iva\emdash and people with a poor fund of knowledge consider Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu no better than Lord Brahm\'e4 or Lord \'c7iva. This conclusion, however, is invalid. As stated in the }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas, i\'f1\'f6\'e4p\'fcrta\'e0 bahudh\'e4 j\'e4yam\'e4na\'e0 vi\'e7va\'e0 bibharti bhuvanasya n\'e4bhi\'f9 tad ev\'e4gnis tad v\'e4yus tat s\'fcryas tad u candram\'e4\'f9 agni\'f9 sarvadaivata\'f9.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  This means that the Supreme Lord, who accepts and enjoys the results of Vedic ritualistic ceremonies (technically called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 i\'f1\'f6\'e4p\'fcrta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
), who maintains the entire creation, who supplies the necessities of all living entities (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 eko bah\'fcn\'e4\'e0 yo vidadh\'e4ti k\'e4m\'e4n}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ) and who is the central 
point of all creation, is Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu expands as the demigods known as Agni, V\'e4yu, S\'fcrya and Candra, who are simply parts and parcels of His body. Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9
mad Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 9.23}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ):
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11741344 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 ye 'py anya-devat\'e4-bhakt\'e4\line yajante \'e7raddhay\'e4nvit\'e4\'f9
\line te 'pi m\'e4m eva kaunteya\line yajanty avidhi-p\'fcrvakam
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"Devotees who worship the demigods with firm faith worship Me also, but not according to regulative principles." In other words, if one worships the demigods but does not understand the relationship between t
he demigods and the Supreme Personality of Godhead, his worship is irregular. K\'e5\'f1\'eba also says in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 9.24}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 aha\'e0 hi sarva-yaj\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'e0 bhokt\'e4 ca prabhur eva ca:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "I am the only enjoyer of ritualistic ceremonies."
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 It may be argued that the demigods are as important as Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u because the names of the demigods are different names of Vi\'f1\'ebu. This, however, is not a sound conclusion, for it is contradicted in the Vedic literatures. The }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  declare:
\par }\pard\plain \s214\qc \fi251\li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11741344 \i\f35\fs24\cf6\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 candram\'e4 ma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11741344 naso j\'e4ta\'e7 cak\'f1o
\'f9 s\'fcryo aj\'e4yata.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  \'e7rotr\'e4daya\'e7 ca pr\'e4\'eba\'e7 }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11741344 \line }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ca mukh\'e4d agnir aj\'e4yata}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11741344 .}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  n\'e4r\'e4ya
\'eb\'e4d brahm\'e4, n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb\'e4d rudro j\'e4yate, }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11741344 \line }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb\'e4t praj\'e4pati\'f9 j\'e4yate, n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb\'e4d indro j\'e4yate, n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb\'e4d a\'f1\'f6au }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11741344 \line }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vasavo j\'e4yante, n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb\'e4d ek\'e4da\'e7a rudr\'e4 j\'e4yante.
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "The demigod of the moon, Candra, came from the mind of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, and the sun-god came from His eyes. The controlling deities of hearing and the life air came from N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, and the controlling deity of fire was generated from His mouth. Praj\'e4pati, Lord Brahm\'e4, came from N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, Indra came from N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, and the eight Vasus, the eleven expansions of Lord \'c7iva and the twelve \'c4dityas also came from N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba." In the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sm\'e5ti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 Vedic literature it is also said:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11741344 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 brahm\'e4 \'e7ambhus tathaiv\'e4rka\'e7\line candram\'e4\'e7 ca \'e7atakratu
\'f9\line evam \'e4dy\'e4s tathaiv\'e4nye\line yukt\'e4 vai\'f1\'ebava-tejas\'e4
\par jagat-k\'e4ry\'e4vas\'e4ne tu\line viyujyante ca tejas\'e4\line viteja\'e7 ca te sarve\line pa\'efcatvam upay\'e4nti te
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "Brahm\'e4, \'c7ambhu, S\'fc
rya and Indra are all merely products of the power of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This is also true of the many other demigods whose names are not mentioned here. When the cosmic manifestation is annihilated, these different expansions of N\'e4r
\'e4ya\'eba's potencies will merge into N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. In other words, all these demigods will die. Their living force will be withdrawn, and they will merge into N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba."
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 Therefore it should be concluded that Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, not Lord Brahm\'e4 or Lord \'c7
iva, is the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As a government officer is sometimes accepted as the entire government although he is actually but a departmental manager, so the demigods, having achieved power of attorney from Vi\'f1\'eb
u, act on His behalf, although they are not as powerful as He. All the demigods must work under the orders of Vi\'f1\'ebu. Therefore it is said, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ekale \'e9\'e7vara k\'e5\'f1\'eba, \'e4ra saba bh\'e5tya.}{
\insrsid11612319  The only master is Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, or Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, and all others are His obedient servants, who act exactly according to His orders. The distinction between Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and the demigods is also expressed in }{
\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid11612319  (9.25). }{\i\insrsid7682563\charrsid7682563 Y}{\i\insrsid11741344\charrsid7682563 \'e4nti deva-vrat\'e4 dev\'e4n...}{\i\insrsid11612319\charrsid7682563 y\'e4nti mad-y\'e4jino 'pi m
\'e4m}{\i\insrsid7682563\charrsid7682563 :}{\i\insrsid7682563  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 those who worship the demigods go to the planets of the demigods, whereas the worshipers of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu go to the planets in Vaiku\'eb
\'f6ha. These are the statements of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sm\'e5ti.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Therefore the idea that Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is on the same level as the demigods is in contradiction to the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
\'e7\'e4stras.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The demigods are not supreme. The supremacy of the demigods is dependent on the mercy of Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba (Vi\'f1\'ebu, or K\'e5\'f1\'eba).
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.20.5
