antra by which the inhabitants of Plak\'f1adv\'e9pa worship the Supreme Lord.}{\fs28\insrsid7682563 ]}{\fs28\insrsid11612319  Let us take shelter of the sun-god, who is a reflection of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, the all-expanding Supreme Personality of Godhead, the oldest of all persons. Vi\'f1\'ebu is the only worshipable Lord. He is the Vedas, He is religion, and He is the origin of all auspicious and inauspicious results.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7682563 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is even the Supreme Lord of death, as confirmed in }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 m\'e5tyu\'f9 sarva-hara\'e7 c\'e4ham}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). There are two kinds of activity\emdash auspicious and inauspicious
\emdash and both are controlled by Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. Inauspicious activities are said to be behind Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, whereas auspicious activities stand before Him. The auspicious and the inauspicious exist throughout the entire world, and Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u is the controller of them both.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In regard to this verse, \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya says:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7682563 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 s\'fcrya-som\'e4gni-v\'e4r\'e9\'e7a-\line vidh\'e4t\'e5\'f1u yath\'e4-kramam
\line plak\'f1\'e4di-dv\'e9pa-sa\'e0sth\'e4su\line sthita\'e0 harim up\'e4sate
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
There are many lands, fields, mountains and oceans throughout the creation, and everywhere the Supreme Personality of Godhead is worshiped by His different names.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9la V\'e9rar\'e4ghava \'c4c\'e4rya explains this verse of }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  as follows. The original cause of the cosmic manifestation must be the oldest person and must therefore be beyond materi
al transformations. He is the enjoyer of all auspicious activities and is the cause of conditional life and also liberation. The demigod S\'fcrya, who is categorized as a very powerful }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 j\'e9va,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or living entity, is a representation of one of the parts of His bod
y. We are naturally subordinate to powerful living entities, and therefore we can worship the various demigods as living beings who are powerful representatives of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Although the worship of the sun-god is recommended in t
his }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mantra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  He is worshiped not as the Supreme Personality of Godhead but as His powerful representative.
\par In the }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Ka\'f6ha Upani\'f1ad}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (1.3.1)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  it is said:
