The sun-god, who controls the affairs of the entire universe, especially in regard to heat, light, seasonal changes and so on, is considered an expansion of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. He represents the three }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 
Vedas-\'c5g, Yajur}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216  and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 S\'e4ma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 -and therefore he is known as Tray\'e9maya, the form of Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a. Sometimes the sun-god is also called S\'fcrya N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. The sun-god has expanded himself in twelve divisions, and thus he controls the six seasonal changes and causes winter, summer, rain and so on. }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 Yog\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216  and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 karm\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216  following the }{
