\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 a\'f1\'f6\'e4\'ecga-yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216  or who perform }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 agnihotra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 
 sacrifices, worship S\'fcrya N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba for their own benefit. The demigod S\'fcrya is always in touch with the Supreme Personality of Godhead, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. Residing in outer space, which is in the middle of the universe, between Bh\'fc
loka and Bhuvarloka, the sun rotates through the time circle of the zodiac, represented by twelve }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 r\'e4\'e7is,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 
 or signs, and assumes different names according to the sig
n he is in. For the moon, every month is divided into two fortnights. Similarly, according to solar calculations, a month is equal to the time the sun spends in one constellation; two months constitute one season, and there are twelve months in a year. Th
e entire area of the sky is divided into two halves, each representing an }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 ayana,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 
 the course traversed by the sun within a period of six months. The sun travels sometimes slowly, sometimes swiftly and sometimes at a moderate speed. In this way it travels wit
hin the three worlds, consisting of the heavenly planets, the earthly planets and outer space. These orbits are referred to by great learned scholars by the names Sa\'e0vatsara, Parivatsara, I\'f2\'e4vatsara, Anuvatsara and Vatsara.
\par The moon is situated 100,000 }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 yojanas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216  above the rays of the sunshine. Day and night on the heavenly planets and Pit\'e5
loka are calculated according to its waning and waxing. Above the moon by a distance of 200,000 }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 yojanas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216  are some stars, and above these stars is \'c7
ukra-graha (Venus), whose influence is always auspicious for the inhabitants of the entire universe. Above \'c7ukra-graha by 200,000 }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 yojanas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 
 is Budha-graha (Mercury), whose influence is sometimes auspicious and sometimes inauspicious. Next, above Budha-graha by 200,000 }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 yojanas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216  is A\'ecg\'e4
raka (Mars), which almost always has an unfavorable influence. Above A\'ecg\'e4raka by another 200,000 }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 yojanas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216  is the planet called B\'e5
haspati-graha (Jupiter), which is always very favorable for qualified }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319\charrsid16650216  Above B\'e5haspati-graha is the planet \'c7anai\'e7cara 
(Saturn), which is very inauspicious, and above Saturn is a group of seven stars occupied by great saintly persons who are always thinking of the welfare of the entire universe. These seven stars circumambulate Dhruvaloka, which is the residence of Lord V
i\'f1\'ebu within this universe.
