u, the soul of all the worlds, is situated in outer space between the upper and lower portions of the universe. Passing through twelve months on the wheel of time, the sun comes in touch with twelve different signs of the zodiac and assumes twelve d
ifferent names according to those signs. The aggregate of those twelve months is called a sa\'e0vatsara, or an entire year. According to lunar calculations, two fortnights\emdash one of the waxing moon and the other of the waning\emdash 
