\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 ha v\'e4va}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash indeed; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 k\'f1uta}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash when in hunger; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 patana}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash falling down; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 praskhalana-\'e4di\'f1u}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash stumbling and so on; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 viva\'e7a\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash being helpless; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 sak\'e5t}{
\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash once; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 n\'e4ma abhig\'e5\'eban}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash chanting the holy name of the Lord; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 puru\'f1a\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash a person; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 karma-bandhanam}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash the bondage of fruitive activity; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 a\'efjas\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash completely; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 vidhunoti}{
\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash washes away; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 yasya}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash of which; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 ha}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash certainly; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 eva}{
\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash in this way; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 pratib\'e4dhanam}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash the repulsion; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 mumuk\'f1ava\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash persons desiring liberation; }{
\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 anyath\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash otherwise; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 eva}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash certainly; }{\cs337\i\fs28\insrsid11612319 upalabhante}{\fs28\insrsid11612319 \emdash 
are trying to realize.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid806975 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11612319 If one who is embarrassed by hunger or who fa
lls down or stumbles chants the holy name of the Lord even once, willingly or unwillingly, he is immediately freed from the reactions of his past deeds. Karm\'e9
s entangled in material activities face many difficulties in the practice of mystic yoga and other endeavors to achieve that same freedom.
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12542146 \b\v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11612319 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
It is not a fact that one has to offer his material possessions to the Supreme Personality of Godhead and be liberated before he can engage in devotional service. A devotee automatically attains liberation without separate endeavors. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja did not get back all his material possessions merely because of his charity to the Lord. One who becomes a devotee, free from material desires and motives, regards all opportunities, both material and spiritual, as 
benedictions from the Lord, and in this way his service to the Lord is never hampered. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhukti,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  material enjoyment, and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mukti,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 liberation, are only by-products of devotional service. A devotee need not work separately to attain }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mukti.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  \'c7r\'e9la Bilvama\'ecgala \'d6h\'e4kura said, }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mukti\'f9 svaya\'e0 mukulit\'e4\'efjali\'f9 sevate 'sm\'e4n:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  a pure devotee of the Lord does not have to endeavor separately for }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mukti,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  because }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 mukti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is always ready to serve him.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 In this regard, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11612319 Antya}{\cf1\insrsid11612319  3.177-188)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  describes Harid\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura's confirmation of the effect of chanting the holy name of the Lord.

\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4540608 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 keha bale\emdash 'n\'e4ma haite haya p\'e4pa-k\'f1aya'\line keha bale\emdash 'n
\'e4ma haite j\'e9vera mok\'f1a haya'
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
Some say that by chanting the holy name of the Lord one is freed from all the reactions of sinful life, and others say that by chanting the holy name of the Lord one attains liberation from material bondage.
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6835955 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 harid\'e4sa kahena,\emdash "n\'e4mera ei dui phala naya\line n\'e4
mera phale k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pade prema upajaya
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Harid\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4
kura, however, said that the desired result of chanting the holy 
name of the Lord is not that one is liberated from material bondage or freed from the reactions of sinful life. The actual result of chanting the holy name of the Lord is that one awakens his dormant K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, his loving service to the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7278246 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e4nu\'f1a\'ecgika phala n\'e4mera\emdash 'mukti', 'p\'e4pa-n\'e4\'e7a'
\line t\'e4h\'e4ra d\'e5\'f1\'f6\'e4nta yaiche s\'fcryera prak\'e4\'e7a
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Harid\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4
kura said that liberation and freedom from the reactions of sinful activities are only by-products of chanting the holy name of the Lord. If one chants the holy na
me of the Lord purely, he attains the platform of loving service to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. In this regard Harid\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura gave an example comparing the power of the holy name to sunshine.
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7278246 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 ei \'e7lokera artha kara pa\'eb\'f2itera ga\'eba"\line sabe kahe,\emdash 
'tumi kaha artha-vivara\'eba'
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
He placed a verse before all the learned scholars present, but the learned scholars asked him to state the purport of the verse.
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7278246 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 harid\'e4sa kahena,\emdash "yaiche s\'fcryera udaya\line udaya n\'e4 haite 
\'e4rambhe tamera haya k\'f1aya
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Harid\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura said tha
t as the sun begins to rise, it dissipates the darkness of night, even before the sunshine is visible.
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7278246 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 caura-preta-r\'e4k\'f1as\'e4dira bhaya haya n\'e4\'e7a\line 
udaya haile dharma-karma-\'e4di parak\'e4\'e7a
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Before the sunrise even takes place, the light of dawn destroys the fear of
