d them. This knowledge is delivered to N\'e4rada by Lord Brahm\'e4, and the great saint N\'e4rada, along with his companion, Tumburu, distributes it all over the universe. Sometimes the Supreme Personality of Godhead is described as Uttama\'e7
loka, one who is praised by beautiful poetry. N\'e4rada composes various poems to glorify Lord Ananta, and therefore the word }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sa\'e0\'e7lokay\'e4m \'e4sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 (praised by selected poetry) is used in this verse.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 The Vai\'f1\'ebavas in the Gau\'f2\'e9ya-samprad\'e4
