\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"The bewildered spirit soul, under the influence of the three modes of material nature, thinks himself to be the doer of activities, whi
ch are in actuality carried out by nature." The foolish person thinks he is independent of any law. He thinks there is no God or regulative principle and that he can do whatever he likes. Thus he engages in different sinful activities, and as a result, he
 
is put into different hellish conditions life after life, to be punished by the laws of nature. The basic principle of his suffering is that he foolishly thinks himself independent, although he is strictly under the control of the laws of material nature.
 
These laws act due to the influence of the three modes of nature, and therefore each human being also works under three different types of influence. According to how he acts, he suffers different reactions in his next life or in this life. Religious pers
ons act differently from atheists, and therefore they suffer different reactions.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 describes the following twenty-eight hells: T\'e4
misra, Andhat\'e4misra, Raurava, Mah\'e4raurava, Kumbh\'e9p\'e4ka. K\'e4las\'fctra, Asi-patravana, S\'fckaramukha, Andhak\'fcpa, K\'e5mibhojana. Sanda\'e0\'e7a, Taptas\'fcrmi, Vajraka\'eb\'f6aka-\'e7\'e4lmal\'e9, Vaitara\'eb\'e9, P\'fcyoda, Pr\'e4\'eb
arodha, Vi\'e7asana, L\'e4l\'e4bhak\'f1a, S\'e4ramey\'e4dana, Av\'e9ci, Aya\'f9p\'e4na. K\'f1\'e4rakardama, Rak\'f1oga\'eba-bhojana, \'c7\'fclaprota, Danda\'e7\'fcka. Ava\'f6a-nirodhana, Pary\'e4vartana and S\'fcc\'e9mukha.
\par A person who steals another's money, wife or possessions is put into the hell known as T\'e4misra. A man who tricks someone and enjoys his wife is put into the extremely hellish condition known as Andhat\'e4
misra. A foolish person absorbed in the bodily concept of life, who on the ba
sis of this principle maintains himself or his wife and children by committing violence against other living entities, is put into the hell known as Raurava. There the animals he killed take birth as creatures called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
rurus}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and cause great suffering for him. Those who kill different animals and birds and then cook them are put by the agents of Yamar\'e4ja into the hell known as Kumbh\'e9p\'e4
ka, where they are boiled in oil. A person who kills a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is put into the hell known as K\'e4las\'fctra, where the land, perfec
tly level and made of copper, is as hot as an oven. The killer of a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 burns in that land for many years. One who does not follow scriptural injunctions but who does everything whimsically or follows some rascal is put into the hell known as Asi-patr
avana. A government official who poorly administers justice, or who punishes an innocent man, is taken by the assistants of Yamar\'e4ja to the hell known as S\'fckaramukha, where he is mercilessly beaten.
\par God has given advanced consciousness to the human being. 
Therefore he can feel the suffering and happiness of other living beings. The human being bereft of his conscience, however, is prone to cause suffering for other living beings. The assistants of Yamar\'e4ja put such a person into the hell known as Andhak
\'fcpa, where he receives proper punishment from his victims. Any person who does not receive or feed a guest properly but who personally enjoys eating is put into the hell known as K\'e5
mibhojana. There an unlimited number of worms and insects continuously bite him.
\par A thief is put into the hell known as Sanda\'e0\'e7a. A person who has sexual relations with a woman who is not to be enjoyed is put into the hell known as Taptas\'fc
rmi. A person who enjoys sexual relations with animals is put into the hell known as Vajraka\'eb\'f6aka-\'e7\'e4lmal\'e9
. A person born into an aristocratic or highly placed family but who does not act accordingly is put into the hellish trench of blood, pus and urine called the Vaitara\'eb\'e9 River. One who lives like an animal is put into the hell called P\'fc
yoda. A person who mercilessly kills animals in the forest without sanction is put into the hell called Pr\'e4\'ebarodha. A person who kills animals in the name of religious sacrifice is put into the hell named Vi\'e7
asana. A man who forces his wife to drink his }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid1909903 semina}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is put into the hell called L\'e4l\'e4bhak\'f1a. One who sets a fire or administers poison to kill someone is put into the hell known as S\'e4ramey
\'e4dana. A man who earns his livelihood by bearing false witness is put into the hell known as Av\'e9ci.
\par A person addicted to drinking wine is put into the hell named Aya\'f9p\'e4na. One who violates etiquette by not showing proper respect to superiors is put into the hell known as K\'f1\'e4
rakardama. A person who sacrifices human beings to Bhairava is put into the hell called Rak\'f1oga\'eba-bhojana. A person who kills pet animals is put into the hell called \'c7\'fc
laprota. A person who gives trouble to others is put into the hell known as Danda\'e7\'fcka. One who imprisons a living entity within a cave is put into the hell known as Ava\'f6a-nirodhana. A person who sh
ows unwarranted wrath toward a guest in his house is put into the hell called Pary\'e4vartana. A person maddened by possessing riches and thus deeply absorbed in thinking of how to collect money is put into the hell known as S\'fcc\'e9mukha.
\par After describing the hellish planets, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 describes how pious persons are elevated to the highest planetary system, where the demigods live, and how they then come back again to this earth when the results of their pious activities are finished. Finally he describes
 the universal form of the Lord and glorifies the Lord's activities.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.26.1
