\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 dharma\'e0 tu s\'e4k\'f1\'e4d bhagavat-pra\'eb\'e9tam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The only religious principle is to follow the orders of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Unfortunately, especially in this age }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid6958466 of Kali, everyone is an atheist. P}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 eople do not even believe in God, what to speak of following His words. The words }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 nija-veda-patha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 can also mean "one's own set of religious principles." Formerly there was only one }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 veda-patha,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 or set of religious principles. Now there are many. It doesn't matter which set of religious principles one follows: the only injunction is that he must follow them strictly. An atheist, or }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 n\'e4stika,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  is one who does not believe in the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Vedas.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 However, even if one takes up a different system of religion, according to this verse he must follow the religious principles he has accepted. Whether one is a Hind
u, or a Mohammedan or a Christian, he should follow his own religious principles. However, if one concocts his own religious path within his mind, or if one follows no religious principles at all, he is punished in the hell known as Asi-patravana. In othe
r
 words, a human being must follow some religious principles. If he does not follow any religious principles, he is no better than an animal. As Kali-yuga advances, people are becoming godless and taking up so-called secularism. They do not know the punish
ment awaiting them in Asi-patravana, as described in this verse.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qj \li0\ri0\sb600\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \v\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11612319 SB 5.26.16
