 necessary, he certainly becomes very proud. This is the situation of men in modern civilization. According to the Vedic culture, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  do not possess anything, whereas }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 k\'f1atriyas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  possess riches, but only for performing sacrifices and other noble activities as prescribed in the Vedic injunctions. A }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vai\'e7ya}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  also earns money honestly through agriculture, cow protection and some trade. If a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7\'fcdra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 gets money, however, he will spend it lavishly, without discrimination, or simply accumulate it for no purpose. Because in this age there are no qualified }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 br\'e4hma\'ebas, k\'f1atriyas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  or }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vai\'e7yas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  almost everyone is a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7\'fcdra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 kalau \'e7\'fcdra-sambhava\'f9}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ). Therefore the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7\'fcdra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  mentality is causing great harm to modern civilization. A }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'e7\'fcdra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
 does not know how to use money to render transcendental loving service to the Lord. Money is also called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 lak\'f1m\'e9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and Lak\'f1m\'e9 is always engaged in the service of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a. Wherever there is money, it must be engaged in the service of Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. Everyone should use his money to spread the great transcendental movement of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness. If one does not spend money for this purpose but accumulates more than necessary, he will certainly become proud of the money he illegally possesses. The money actually belongs to K\'e5\'f1\'eba, who says in }{
\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 5.29}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ), }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 bhokt\'e4ra\'e0 yaj\'efa-tapas\'e4\'e0 sarva-loka-mahe\'e7varam:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "I am the true enjoyer of sacrifices and penances, and I am the owner of all the planets." Therefore nothing belongs to anyone but K\'e5\'f1\'eba. One who possesses more money than he needs should spend it for K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. Unless one does so, he will become puffed up because of his false possessions, and therefore he will be punished in the next life, as described herein.
