\par }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 There is a supplementary note written by His Divine Grace Bhaktisiddh\'e4nta Sarasvat\'e9 Gosv\'e4m\'e9 Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Prabhup\'e4da in his }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Gau\'f2\'e9ya-bh\'e4\'f1ya.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Its translation is as follows. Learned scholars who have full knowledge of all the Vedic script
ures agree that the incarnations of the Supreme Personality of Godhead are innumerable. These incarnations are classified into two divisions, called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 pr\'e4bhava}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 vaibhava.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  According to the scriptures, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 pr\'e4bhava}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  incarnations are also classified in two divisions\emdash 
those which are called eternal and those which are not vividly described. In this Fifth Canto of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  in Chapters Three through Six, there is a description of \'c5\'f1
abhadeva, but there is not an expanded description of His spiritual activities. Therefore He is considered to belong to the second group of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 pr\'e4bhava}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  incarnations. In }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  First Canto, Chapter Three, verse 13}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4025764 , i}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 t is said:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12218116 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 a\'f1\'f6ame merudevy\'e4\'e0 tu\line n\'e4bher j\'e4ta urukrama\'f9\line 
dar\'e7ayan vartma dh\'e9r\'e4\'eb\'e4\'e0\line sarv\'e4\'e7rama-namask\'e5tam
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu appeared in the eighth incarnation as the son of Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja N\'e4bhi }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid12218116 [}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 the son of \'c4gn\'e9dhra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid12218116 ]}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  and his wife Merudev\'e9. He showed the path of perfection, the }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 paramaha\'e0sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  stage of life, which is worshiped by all the followers of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 "}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid12218116 
 }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c5\'f1abhadeva is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and His body is spiritual (}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
). Therefore one might ask how it might be possible that he passed stool and urine. The Gau\'f2\'e9ya }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ved\'e4nta \'e4c\'e4rya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  Baladeva Vidy\'e4bh\'fc\'f1a\'eb
a has replied to this question in his book known as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Siddh\'e4nta-ratna}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (First Portion, texts 65-68). Imperfect men call attention to \'c5\'f1
abhadeva's passing stool and urine as a subject matter for the study of nondevotees, who do not understand the spiritual position of a transcendental body. In this Fifth Canto of }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (5.6.11)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  the illusioned and bewildered state of the materialists of this age is fully described. Elsewhere in Fifth Canto }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (5.5.19)}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  \'c5\'f1abhadeva stated, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ida\'e0 \'e7ar\'e9ram mama durvibh\'e4vyam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  "This body of Mine is inconceivable for materialists." This is also confirmed by Lord K\'e5\'f1
\'eba in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  (}{\cf1\insrsid11612319 9.11}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 ):
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12218116 \i\f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11612319 avaj\'e4nanti m\'e4\'e0 m\'fc\'f2h\'e4\line m\'e4nu\'f1\'e9\'e0 tanum \'e4
\'e7ritam\line para\'e0 bh\'e4vam aj\'e4nanto\line mama bh\'fcta-mahe\'e7varam
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
"Fools deride Me when I descend in the human form. They do not know My transcendental nature a
nd My supreme dominion over all that be." The human form of the Supreme Personality of Godhead is extremely difficult to understand, and, in fact, for a common man it is inconceivable. Therefore \'c5\'f1
abhadeva has directly explained that His own body belongs to the sp}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11410444 iritual platform. This being so,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  \'c5\'f1
abhadeva did not actually pass stool and urine. Even though He superficially seemed to pass stool and urine, that was also transcendental and cannot be imitated by any common man. It is also stated in }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh
\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  that the stool and urine of \'c5\'f1abhadeva were full of transcendental fragrance. One may imitate \'c5\'f1abhadeva, but he cannot imitate Him by passing stool that is fragrant.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 The activities of \'c5\'f1
abhadeva, therefore, do not support the claims of a certain class of men known as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 arhat,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  who sometimes advertise that they are followers of \'c5\'f1abhadeva. How can they be followers of \'c5
\'f1abhadeva while they act against the Vedic principles? \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 has related that after hearing about the characteristics of Lord \'c5\'f1abhadeva, the King of Ko\'ecka, Ve\'ecka and Ku\'f6
aka initiated a system of religious principles known as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 arhat.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  These principles were not in accord with Vedic principles, and therefore they are called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 p
\'e4\'f1a\'eb\'f2a-dharma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  The members of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 arhat}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  community considered \'c5\'f1abhadeva's activities material. However, \'c5\'f1
abhadeva is an incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore He is on the transcendental platform, and no one can compare to Him.
\par \'c5\'f1abhadeva personally exhibited the activities of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As stated in }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  }{\cf1\insrsid11612319 (5.6.8)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 
, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 d\'e4v\'e4nalas tad vanam \'e4lelih\'e4na\'f9 saha tena dad\'e4ha:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  at the conclusion of \'c5\'f1
abhadeva's pastimes, an entire forest and the Lord's body were burned to ashes in a great forest fire. In the same way, \'c5\'f1abhadeva burned people's ignorance to ashes. He exhibited the characteristics of a }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 paramaha
\'e0sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  in His instructions to His sons. The principles of the }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 arhat}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  community, however, do not correspond to the teachings of \'c5\'f1abhadeva.
\par \'c7r\'e9la Baladeva Vidy\'e4bh\'fc\'f1a\'eba remarks that in the Eighth Canto of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319  there is another description of \'c5\'f1abhadeva, but that \'c5\'f1
abhadeva is different from the one described in this canto.
\par }\pard\plain \s66\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9198789 \b\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11612319 END OF THE FIFTH CANTO}{\insrsid11612319 
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid9464468 
\par }\pard\plain \s271\qj \li0\ri0\sb240\sa240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9535257 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid9464468 SYNONYMS}{\insrsid9464468 
